WEBVTT

00:34.542 --> 00:37.167
[seagulls squawking faintly]

00:37.917 --> 00:40.208
[pensive atmospheric music]

00:55.000 --> 00:57.458
[pensive music continues]

00:58.083 --> 01:00.417
[soft buzzing, faintly]

01:09.042 --> 01:11.625
[soft buzzing]

01:12.125 --> 01:15.416
[female voice, on app]<i>The cat prefers blue pyjamas.</i>

01:15.417 --> 01:17.957
<i>Le chat préfère
les pyjamas bleus.</i>

01:17.958 --> 01:20.542
[man] Le chat préfère
les pyjamas bleus.

01:23.458 --> 01:25.874
[female voice, on app]<i>The cat eats pizza on the bus.</i>

01:25.875 --> 01:28.666
<i>Le chat mange de la pizza
dans le bus.</i>

01:28.667 --> 01:31.166
[man] Le chat mange de la pizza
dans le bus.

01:31.167 --> 01:32.916
[soft buzzing continues]

01:32.917 --> 01:34.750
[cell phone chimes]

01:44.750 --> 01:46.375
[cell phone whoops]

02:03.250 --> 02:06.249
[cell phone ringing]

02:06.250 --> 02:07.541
[man on phone] <i>G'day, Hank.</i>

02:07.542 --> 02:09.499
<i>Has my favourite runner
finished brekky yet?</i>

02:09.500 --> 02:10.874
<i>Because it's go time!</i>

02:10.875 --> 02:12.416
I don't clock in
for an hour, Iggy.

02:12.417 --> 02:14.707
- Got an appointment at 7, so...<i>-Oh, yeah, that's right.</i>

02:14.708 --> 02:16.166
<i>Well, as soon as you're done,</i>

02:16.167 --> 02:18.541
<i>I need my "big American
war hero" in top form.</i>

02:18.542 --> 02:20.541
<i>We have a couple of tricky
clients this morning, mate,</i>

02:20.542 --> 02:22.874
<i>so I need you to be
at the top of your game.</i>

02:22.875 --> 02:24.374
<i>- I don't want any excuses.</i>
- OK.

02:24.375 --> 02:26.082
<i>We have got money to make,
and you are...</i>

02:26.083 --> 02:28.249
- Iggy, I got it, I got it.<i>-..my number one money maker.</i>

02:28.250 --> 02:29.874
I'll be ready after
the appointment,

02:29.875 --> 02:31.208
not a second sooner.

02:33.000 --> 02:34.667
[engine revs]

02:37.917 --> 02:40.708
That's right, John.
Thank you for sharing.

02:41.500 --> 02:42.666
Ladies and gents,

02:42.667 --> 02:45.708
we have a very special
sober birthday today.

02:47.958 --> 02:49.625
Our resident Yank.

02:51.750 --> 02:53.832
- [man] Congratulations, Hank.
- Thank you.

02:53.833 --> 02:55.291
Good on ya, buddy.

02:55.292 --> 02:58.125
[attendees clapping]

03:01.833 --> 03:05.792
[wistful atmospheric music]

03:16.333 --> 03:18.707
[cell phone ringing]

03:18.708 --> 03:20.333
[engine starting up]

03:21.875 --> 03:22.999
[Hank] OK, Iggy.

03:23.000 --> 03:24.457
[Iggy] <i>You're out of
your meeting?</i>

03:24.458 --> 03:26.666
- [Hank] Yep.<i>-Great. You ready to rock?</i>

03:26.667 --> 03:28.416
[Hank] Sure.
What's the itinerary?

03:28.417 --> 03:30.041
["Spirit in the Sky" plays]

03:30.042 --> 03:31.957
<i>First one I think
you're gonna love.</i>

03:31.958 --> 03:33.499
<i>Some senior minister,</i>

03:33.500 --> 03:36.207
<i>who's supposed to vote on
a major cabinet decision today,</i>

03:36.208 --> 03:38.332
<i>- has apparently gone walkabout.</i>
- [elevator dings]

03:38.333 --> 03:40.624
<i>But my guy,
Detective Manoa,</i>

03:40.625 --> 03:43.374
<i>has tracked him down
in some fancy hotel.</i>

03:43.375 --> 03:45.374
Cops on payroll now, huh?

03:45.375 --> 03:46.999
Moving up in the world, Iggy.

03:47.000 --> 03:49.457
Why not just have your tickle
buddy Manoa handle it, then?

03:49.458 --> 03:52.124
<i>That's 'cause the government
wants it off book, mate.</i>

03:52.125 --> 03:53.416
<i>Oh, and, Hank?</i>

03:53.417 --> 03:55.374
- [woman giggling]<i>-You've got the green light</i>

03:55.375 --> 03:57.624
<i>to do whatever it takes.</i>

03:57.625 --> 03:59.582
- I don't hurt people anymore.<i>-Oh, yeah?</i>

03:59.583 --> 04:01.457
<i>Well, I got a text here
that literally reads,</i>

04:01.458 --> 04:04.791
<i>"Premier said runner
can kick arse if necessary."</i>

04:04.792 --> 04:06.624
- [snoring]
- I gotta go.

04:06.625 --> 04:09.832
<i>♪ When I die
and they lay me to rest ♪</i>

04:09.833 --> 04:14.041
<i>♪ Gonna go to the place
that's the best ♪</i>

04:14.042 --> 04:16.749
<i>♪ When they lay me down
to die ♪</i>

04:16.750 --> 04:21.332
<i>♪ Goin' up to the spirit
in the sky ♪</i>

04:21.333 --> 04:23.917
[grunts, groans wearily]

04:24.583 --> 04:27.332
Up. Up, up, up, up, up,
up, up, up, up, up.

04:27.333 --> 04:28.999
[both grunt]

04:29.000 --> 04:30.624
[minister gasps]

04:30.625 --> 04:32.291
[exhales]

04:32.292 --> 04:34.208
[slurring] I'm sorry.

04:35.417 --> 04:36.999
Will you hold me?

04:37.000 --> 04:39.707
[mumbling, groaning]

04:39.708 --> 04:41.332
- Let's go.
- Oh...

04:41.333 --> 04:44.249
[Iggy] <i>This next one involves
some hotshot tech CEO's bird.</i>

04:44.250 --> 04:45.541
Wait, bird?

04:45.542 --> 04:47.707
<i>I don't know.
Yeah, just do whatever he says.</i>

04:47.708 --> 04:49.500
Iggy, did you say "bird"?

04:50.458 --> 04:52.207
- [bird squawks]
- Here she is.

04:52.208 --> 04:53.541
[squawks]

04:53.542 --> 04:54.666
It's going to my bitch ex-wife.

04:54.667 --> 04:56.041
She got him in the divorce.

04:56.042 --> 04:58.291
- Careful, though. She's beaky!
- Beaky?

04:58.292 --> 05:00.624
OK, I'm in the middle of a
meditation, so I really have--

05:00.625 --> 05:02.832
Whoa, whoa... Why isn't
animal control handling this?

05:02.833 --> 05:04.791
'Cause it's
a Queen Bavaria conure.

05:04.792 --> 05:06.624
What does that...?
I don't know birds.

05:06.625 --> 05:08.999
It's an endangered parakeet.

05:09.000 --> 05:10.749
Endangered, like illegal?

05:10.750 --> 05:12.749
What I'm saying is,
it's worth a fortune.

05:12.750 --> 05:15.832
It was either give her
the <i>FUCKING BIRD</i>

05:15.833 --> 05:17.332
or the Bentley.

05:17.333 --> 05:18.500
Cheers, mate.

05:19.792 --> 05:20.999
Namaste.

05:21.000 --> 05:22.332
<i>♪ Prepare yourself ♪</i>

05:22.333 --> 05:24.332
<i>- ♪ You know it's a must ♪</i>
- Namaste.

05:24.333 --> 05:28.249
<i>♪ Gotta have a friend
in Jesus ♪</i>

05:28.250 --> 05:31.541
<i>♪ So you know that
when you die ♪</i>

05:31.542 --> 05:35.374
<i>♪ He's gonna recommend you
to the spirit in the sky ♪</i>

05:35.375 --> 05:38.291
<i>♪ Whoa, he'll recommend you
to the spirit in the sky ♪</i>

05:38.292 --> 05:39.749
<i>♪ (Spirit in the sky) ♪</i>

05:39.750 --> 05:42.332
<i>♪ That's where you're gonna go
when you die ♪</i>

05:42.333 --> 05:43.666
<i>♪ (When you die) ♪</i>

05:43.667 --> 05:46.207
<i>♪ When you die
and they lay you to rest ♪</i>

05:46.208 --> 05:48.666
<i>♪ You're gonna go to the place
that's the best ♪</i>

05:48.667 --> 05:50.041
[buzzes intercom]

05:50.042 --> 05:51.707
[woman, over intercom]<i>What do you want?</i>

05:51.708 --> 05:53.666
Uh, yeah, I got your
parakeet thing?

05:53.667 --> 05:55.666
<i>You tell Daryl
I don't want that bird,</i>

05:55.667 --> 05:57.124
<i>I want the Bentley!</i>

05:57.125 --> 05:58.499
You're not gettin' the Bentley!

05:58.500 --> 06:00.416
<i>Oh, yeah? Fuck you!</i>

06:00.417 --> 06:02.416
[Daryl] You haven't done that
in years, ya moll!

06:02.417 --> 06:05.207
<i>I wouldn't touch you if you
were the last thing on Earth!</i>

06:05.208 --> 06:07.666
Oh, yeah? Well, I'd rather
do anything else but you!

06:07.667 --> 06:09.291
<i>Then shove that bird
up your arse!</i>

06:09.292 --> 06:11.499
Can you just... just tell me
what to do with the bird?!

06:11.500 --> 06:13.207
- Kill it!<i>-Keep it!</i>

06:13.208 --> 06:14.457
[sighs]

06:14.458 --> 06:15.583
[bird squawks]

06:16.417 --> 06:19.125
- [water lapping gently]
- [sirens in distance]

06:20.792 --> 06:23.792
- [soft music]
- [exhales gently]

06:27.292 --> 06:30.541
[line ringing]

06:30.542 --> 06:31.791
[clears throat]

06:31.792 --> 06:34.042
[line continues ringing]

06:34.917 --> 06:36.832
[Monica on phone] <i>Hi, Hank.</i>

06:36.833 --> 06:38.291
Hey, Mon.

06:38.292 --> 06:40.000
<i>What's going on?</i>

06:41.000 --> 06:43.207
I was just, um...

06:43.208 --> 06:45.333
I was calling 'cause, uh...

06:46.583 --> 06:49.125
...I got my one year coin today.

06:50.542 --> 06:53.000
And I...
I guess I just, yeah...

06:55.583 --> 06:57.374
...wanted you to know.

06:57.375 --> 06:58.750
<i>Oh.</i>

06:59.667 --> 07:03.207
<i>Well, that's... that's really
good to hear, Hank.</i>

07:03.208 --> 07:05.292
<i>You've worked really hard
for that.</i>

07:06.625 --> 07:08.166
- Yeah, um...
- [baby crying over phone]

07:08.167 --> 07:10.332
[Monica] <i>Hey there, hey, hey.
Come on, come on.</i>

07:10.333 --> 07:12.207
<i>Come to Mommy. Come on.</i>

07:12.208 --> 07:15.332
<i>- Shh. It's OK.</i>
- [crying dims]

07:15.333 --> 07:16.957
- How are you?<i>-I'm fine.</i>

07:16.958 --> 07:19.041
<i>The baby's keeping me up most
nights, and I swear I don't</i>

07:19.042 --> 07:21.624
<i>remember you and I ever being
this knackered with Isabel.</i>

07:21.625 --> 07:23.499
<i>She was always so...</i>

07:23.500 --> 07:25.916
- Mellow?<i>-Yeah.</i>

07:25.917 --> 07:27.207
[door clicking over phone]

07:27.208 --> 07:29.916
<i>Um, listen, Josh just got home.
I've gotta go.</i>

07:29.917 --> 07:33.500
<i>Congratulations, Hank.
I'm... I'm happy for you.</i>

07:36.792 --> 07:38.250
[inhales]

07:39.458 --> 07:40.917
[sighs deeply]

07:43.625 --> 07:46.333
[cell phone ringing]

07:49.583 --> 07:51.749
Iggy, please,
just let me eat my lunch.

07:51.750 --> 07:54.124
[Iggy] <i>Mate, I'm sorry,
but something's just come in</i>

07:54.125 --> 07:55.791
<i>that's a huge pay day.</i>

07:55.792 --> 07:57.457
<i>And it's very time sensitive.</i>

07:57.458 --> 07:59.124
<i>So we gotta
move on it right now.</i>

07:59.125 --> 08:01.082
<i>But it should be
really easy, Hank.</i>

08:01.083 --> 08:03.582
- Fine, I'm listening.<i>-OK, as we speak,</i>

08:03.583 --> 08:06.749
<i>there's a private jet heading
from Honolulu to Brisbane</i>

08:06.750 --> 08:10.166
<i>with a highly sensitive
medical package on board.</i>

08:10.167 --> 08:13.416
<i>All you gotta do
is pick it up at 3 o'clock.</i>

08:13.417 --> 08:15.041
<i>Not a second later, Hank.</i>

08:15.042 --> 08:16.874
<i>And just drive it
straight to Albany Creek.</i>

08:16.875 --> 08:18.832
What do you mean by
"medical package"?

08:18.833 --> 08:20.249
[bird squawks]

08:20.250 --> 08:23.082
["Long Cool Woman
in a Black Dress" plays]

08:23.083 --> 08:26.374
<i>♪ She was a long cool woman
in a black dress... ♪</i>

08:26.375 --> 08:28.499
[man] Wait a second -
you've got a layover

08:28.500 --> 08:30.999
on one of the most beautiful
coastlines in the world

08:31.000 --> 08:32.624
and you don't have any plans?

08:32.625 --> 08:33.999
[woman] No, I don't.

08:34.000 --> 08:36.582
Look, I understand
that the ink is barely dry

08:36.583 --> 08:38.707
and divorce can seem
like an ending,

08:38.708 --> 08:41.791
but you gotta look at it
as a beginning.

08:41.792 --> 08:44.291
Audrey, trust me.
I've had three of 'em.

08:44.292 --> 08:46.249
You're gonna love it,
I promise you.

08:46.250 --> 08:48.374
- But you gotta get out there.
- I don't know, Ben.

08:48.375 --> 08:51.874
Room service and an early night
sounds pretty good right now.

08:51.875 --> 08:53.999
No, no,
I cannot let you do that.

08:54.000 --> 08:56.416
It sounds like a defeat, and
I want you to have a victory.

08:56.417 --> 08:58.082
Hey, you know what?

08:58.083 --> 08:59.707
After I make this delivery,

08:59.708 --> 09:02.374
I'm gonna drive back to
Brisbane and we all go out.

09:02.375 --> 09:04.416
But you were gonna go see
the Great Barrier Reef.

09:04.417 --> 09:05.541
I've seen it!

09:05.542 --> 09:07.291
Plus, when you got
a man overboard,

09:07.292 --> 09:08.999
you gotta keep plans fluid!

09:09.000 --> 09:10.207
[Ben chuckles]

09:10.208 --> 09:12.582
And there's this great
seafood restaurant

09:12.583 --> 09:16.457
that has these beautiful
little angasi oysters

09:16.458 --> 09:18.707
that they pair with
a Chardonnay from Tasmania

09:18.708 --> 09:20.541
that made me feel like
I was gonna go blind

09:20.542 --> 09:22.832
- after I drank it.
- Wow, you're a foodie?

09:22.833 --> 09:25.541
Not a foodie, I'm a bon vivant.

09:25.542 --> 09:27.166
- [chuckles]
- [Ben] Big difference.

09:27.167 --> 09:29.083
So, what do ya say?

09:30.500 --> 09:31.957
OK, I'm in.

09:31.958 --> 09:33.624
Yes! She's in!

09:33.625 --> 09:35.291
All right!
I will see you later.

09:35.292 --> 09:38.124
And, listen, a mother
and her little daughter

09:38.125 --> 09:39.917
thank all of you guys.

09:41.833 --> 09:43.416
We're heroes today.

09:43.417 --> 09:45.541
<i>- ♪ One look I was a bad mess ♪</i>
- Hey.

09:45.542 --> 09:47.457
How you doin'? Thank you.
Great to be here.

09:47.458 --> 09:50.707
<i>♪ 'Cause that long cool woman
had it all. ♪</i>

09:50.708 --> 09:55.291
So it doesn't live in the sky,
in the ocean or on land,

09:55.292 --> 09:57.707
but it can travel
through all three?

09:57.708 --> 09:59.332
[monitor beeping steadily]

09:59.333 --> 10:02.332
And you're sure it's not...

10:02.333 --> 10:05.457
a flying monkey
with fish gills?!

10:05.458 --> 10:08.416
- I'm sure.
- But it does have wings?

10:08.417 --> 10:09.957
How big?

10:09.958 --> 10:11.624
[gasps theatrically]

10:11.625 --> 10:13.166
Wowee!

10:13.167 --> 10:15.666
Mom, I'm tired.

10:15.667 --> 10:17.458
It's OK.

10:20.750 --> 10:23.292
[fondly] That's enough for now.
Yeah.

10:24.750 --> 10:26.000
[kisses repeatedly]

10:28.583 --> 10:31.542
[gentle, tender music]

10:33.250 --> 10:34.874
[gasps]

10:34.875 --> 10:36.583
[sighs, sniffles]

10:38.667 --> 10:39.875
[exhales heavily]

10:41.708 --> 10:44.250
Kate. Can I have a word?

10:46.000 --> 10:50.416
So, I got a call from Kuakini
Medical Center in Honolulu.

10:50.417 --> 10:52.374
I didn't want to tell you
any of this

10:52.375 --> 10:55.250
until I was absolutely sure,
but now I am.

10:56.250 --> 10:57.916
We have a match, Kate.

10:57.917 --> 10:59.208
[gasps]

10:59.917 --> 11:01.541
Now, the liver
was supposed to come

11:01.542 --> 11:02.791
straight to the Gold Coast,

11:02.792 --> 11:04.416
but they had to be
redirected to Brisbane,

11:04.417 --> 11:05.957
where a private courier -

11:05.958 --> 11:08.499
who I have been assured
is the cream of the crop -

11:08.500 --> 11:10.750
will pick it up
and drive it straight to us.

11:12.792 --> 11:14.666
[female voice, on app]<i>Imagine that your throat</i>

11:14.667 --> 11:15.999
<i>is a disposal drain.</i>

11:16.000 --> 11:17.666
<i>Now say "rouge".</i>

11:17.667 --> 11:19.999
- [trilling] Rouge. Rouge.
- [blues rock music]

11:20.000 --> 11:22.500
<i>♪ I've been everywhere ♪</i>

11:23.333 --> 11:24.874
<i>♪ A-go, go, go, go ♪</i>

11:24.875 --> 11:27.458
<i>♪ I'm a one-man train... ♪</i>

11:28.458 --> 11:30.041
[Ben] Hank?

11:30.042 --> 11:32.249
You're Hank, aren't you?
I knew it.

11:32.250 --> 11:34.457
Hank is a "big guy" name.

11:34.458 --> 11:38.166
There you go. How you doin'?
Ben Bishop. You ready?

11:38.167 --> 11:40.749
Sure.
I can take it now, Mr Bishop.

11:40.750 --> 11:43.124
Call me "Ben".
Mr Bishop was my father's name.

11:43.125 --> 11:44.749
Sure. Can I have it?

11:44.750 --> 11:47.624
- You already do.
- What are you talking about?

11:47.625 --> 11:50.291
You're delivering <i>me.
I'm</i> delivering something.

11:50.292 --> 11:52.291
You see, this is
a state-of-the-art,

11:52.292 --> 11:55.166
temperature-controlled
organ preservation system.

11:55.167 --> 11:57.624
<i>Hermano,</i> this is not
a FedEx package.

11:57.625 --> 12:00.791
So, today, you get to be the
delivery man's delivery man.

12:00.792 --> 12:02.791
- Copy that?
- Not really.

12:02.792 --> 12:04.541
All right, we're off
like a prom dress.

12:04.542 --> 12:06.624
You got one of those smart
thingies right there, right?

12:06.625 --> 12:08.082
So what we're gonna do,

12:08.083 --> 12:10.541
we're gonna set a halfway mark
and a final mark alarm.

12:10.542 --> 12:12.332
At the halfway mark,
we call the doctor,

12:12.333 --> 12:14.999
let her know we're on target
for a 5 o'clock arrival

12:15.000 --> 12:17.541
and just lower everybody's
blood pressure.

12:17.542 --> 12:19.374
The only one who's worked up
right now is you.

12:19.375 --> 12:21.832
Yeah, probably. That's how
I get when I'm excited.

12:21.833 --> 12:23.458
I'll get us there
in 15 minutes.

12:24.292 --> 12:26.332
It's 15 minutes
to the Gold Coast Hospital?

12:26.333 --> 12:28.041
No - I was told
we were delivering this

12:28.042 --> 12:30.249
- to Albany Creek.
- No. What, what...?

12:30.250 --> 12:31.874
OK, thank God I'm here.

12:31.875 --> 12:33.666
Listen, this isn't me
coming down on you.

12:33.667 --> 12:36.541
What happens is,
people start playing telephone,

12:36.542 --> 12:39.082
one guy says Beverly Boulevard,
the other says Beverly Drive.

12:39.083 --> 12:40.957
- I know what I was told.
- And things get screwed up.

12:40.958 --> 12:42.624
I know what I heard.
I heard Albany Creek.

12:42.625 --> 12:44.249
Gold Coast Hospital.
End of story.

12:44.250 --> 12:46.791
Let me do my job, OK,
and then you can do yours.

12:46.792 --> 12:48.832
Now, you want me
in the front or the back?

12:48.833 --> 12:50.457
You want me in the back, right?

12:50.458 --> 12:52.374
'Cause you like
your own damn space. OK.

12:52.375 --> 12:54.916
But, hey, don't be
surprised if you're begging me

12:54.917 --> 12:56.582
to ride shotgun.

12:56.583 --> 12:59.167
But I won't do it, 'cause
I think better in the back.

13:00.333 --> 13:03.332
Uh, Hank? You already got
a passenger back here.

13:03.333 --> 13:05.499
- [bird squawks]
- It's a long story.

13:05.500 --> 13:06.832
[Ben] I bet.

13:06.833 --> 13:09.499
- Well, I like long stories.
- [cell phone whoops]

13:09.500 --> 13:12.416
[Ben, fondly] Oh! Hello!

13:12.417 --> 13:14.249
Why is 5 the magic number?

13:14.250 --> 13:17.374
Well, actually, 5:45 is
the magic number.

13:17.375 --> 13:20.707
But I just say 5 to give us
a little breathing room.

13:20.708 --> 13:23.666
You see, organs have
a window of viability.

13:23.667 --> 13:26.332
And because we're
coming in from Honolulu,

13:26.333 --> 13:28.374
we're already running
a little bit behind.

13:28.375 --> 13:29.666
But it's OK.

13:29.667 --> 13:31.625
[engine revs]

13:32.583 --> 13:34.624
[Hank] What happens after 5:45?

13:34.625 --> 13:38.291
After 5:45, the chances of
the body accepting the organ

13:38.292 --> 13:40.917
get a... well, it gets
a little trickier.

13:42.042 --> 13:43.416
[engine starting up]

13:43.417 --> 13:46.458
[low foreboding music]

13:50.125 --> 13:54.083
[soft, ethereal vocalising]

13:56.708 --> 13:58.624
Hey, do you ever have that?

13:58.625 --> 14:00.707
Where you're, like,
so exhausted

14:00.708 --> 14:02.666
that you're actually
kinda wired?

14:02.667 --> 14:04.000
That's where I'm at.

14:06.208 --> 14:08.042
You're not very chatty,
are you?

14:09.000 --> 14:10.749
- No.
- [chuckles]

14:10.750 --> 14:12.666
That's gonna be
a little bit of a problem.

14:12.667 --> 14:15.624
Only because
I kinda talk a lot.

14:15.625 --> 14:17.332
But why don't we do this?

14:17.333 --> 14:19.541
I'm gonna dial it
down a little bit,

14:19.542 --> 14:21.916
and you crank it way up,
and we meet in the middle.

14:21.917 --> 14:23.666
- How's that sound?
- I don't mean to be rude--

14:23.667 --> 14:25.416
You know, my first ex-wife
used to say

14:25.417 --> 14:28.207
you can divide the world
into two different buckets.

14:28.208 --> 14:29.624
Bucket number one,

14:29.625 --> 14:33.291
they're drinking that Ben
Bishop Kool-Aid, glug, glug.

14:33.292 --> 14:35.207
And then, the other one?

14:35.208 --> 14:38.124
Too much sugar, yeah.
Starts to make 'em sick.

14:38.125 --> 14:40.124
I don't know, you could be
in bucket number two,

14:40.125 --> 14:41.416
it's too early to tell.

14:41.417 --> 14:42.791
But that's all right.

14:42.792 --> 14:44.541
That's where the ex-wives
usually ended up.

14:44.542 --> 14:46.291
But, guess what,
I think I'm gonna win you over.

14:46.292 --> 14:49.000
- Hey, listen, Mr Bishop--
- Oh, Iggy's calling.

14:50.500 --> 14:52.291
- Yeah?
- [Iggy] <i>Update me, mate.</i>

14:52.292 --> 14:54.916
- I picked him up.<i>-Him?</i>

14:54.917 --> 14:56.666
Yeah, the medical courier.
Ben Bishop.

14:56.667 --> 14:59.082
<i>Who the fuck
is Ben Bishop, Hank?</i>

14:59.083 --> 15:01.457
<i>You're just supposed
to pick up a package.</i>

15:01.458 --> 15:02.666
He <i>is</i> the package.

15:02.667 --> 15:04.332
The total package.

15:04.333 --> 15:06.332
He transports the organ,
I transport him.

15:06.333 --> 15:08.457
You booked this thing. Why
am I explaining this to you?

15:08.458 --> 15:11.082
[uneasily] <i>OK... All right.
Um, where are ya, mate?</i>

15:11.083 --> 15:12.707
I already told ya,
I'm on the way.

15:12.708 --> 15:15.582
<i>No, I mean specifically, Hank.
Where are you specifically?</i>

15:15.583 --> 15:17.791
I'm in the Clem7 Tunnel, OK?

15:17.792 --> 15:19.749
<i>Clem7? What are you doing
on the Clem7, Hank?!</i>

15:19.750 --> 15:21.707
<i>- You need to be on the M1!</i>
- Iggy, calm down!

15:21.708 --> 15:23.832
The address you gave me
is wrong, all right?

15:23.833 --> 15:25.874
We're going to the
Gold Coast Hospital.

15:25.875 --> 15:27.582
We're on our way there.
What's the problem?

15:27.583 --> 15:29.666
<i>Look, just go to the address
I fucking gave you</i>

15:29.667 --> 15:31.166
<i>and stop fuckin' about!</i>

15:31.167 --> 15:34.207
Hey, hey, whoa... Hey, Iggy?
It's the total package here.

15:34.208 --> 15:37.124
With all due respect,
I'm in charge here today, OK?

15:37.125 --> 15:39.332
So the address
isn't up for debate.

15:39.333 --> 15:41.291
You had it wrong,
we corrected it.

15:41.292 --> 15:42.874
Problem solved. Copy?

15:42.875 --> 15:47.249
<i>Uh, OK, look, I gotta go.
Just stay by your phone, Hank.</i>

15:47.250 --> 15:50.292
<i>- You got a fortune in that car.</i>
- Wait, what did you just say?

15:51.708 --> 15:55.167
Oh. My, you got a real
crankopotamus there.

15:57.292 --> 15:58.332
[engine starting up]

15:58.333 --> 16:00.333
The plan's changed. Gotta go.

16:01.667 --> 16:03.457
[bikers chattering
indistinctly]

16:03.458 --> 16:04.958
[engine revs]

16:06.250 --> 16:09.083
[bikers chattering
indistinctly]

16:13.292 --> 16:15.082
OK, everything good
on this end,

16:15.083 --> 16:18.624
which gives us time to circle
back to hearing about the bird.

16:18.625 --> 16:20.416
'Cause we got a lot of time.

16:20.417 --> 16:22.166
Why don't you just let me
eat my lunch first?

16:22.167 --> 16:23.832
Be a lot easier to talk
once I've eaten.

16:23.833 --> 16:25.582
Yeah, I get like that too.

16:25.583 --> 16:27.207
What kind of sandwich
you having?

16:27.208 --> 16:28.332
[sighs]

16:28.333 --> 16:29.707
It's a croque monsieur.

16:29.708 --> 16:31.541
[Ben] Oh, a French sandwich!

16:31.542 --> 16:33.999
And you're learning French.
That's unusual.

16:34.000 --> 16:36.124
Are you a Francophile?

16:36.125 --> 16:37.749
How'd you know I study French?

16:37.750 --> 16:40.124
Because of the app
on your phone.

16:40.125 --> 16:41.499
[bird] Peekaboo!

16:41.500 --> 16:43.832
Are you...? Did you hear that?!

16:43.833 --> 16:45.791
[stammers] He can talk!

16:45.792 --> 16:48.166
Did you teach him to talk? Huh?

16:48.167 --> 16:49.457
Can you say it again?

16:49.458 --> 16:51.124
- Peekaboo!
- [bird] Peekaboo!

16:51.125 --> 16:54.082
[laughing] This is
the best day of my life!

16:54.083 --> 16:56.457
We could make some money
on this. We gotta name him.

16:56.458 --> 16:58.041
What's his name?
Let's call him Spirit.

16:58.042 --> 16:59.666
Spirit! One more time.

16:59.667 --> 17:01.374
Can you two cut that out?
That's enough.

17:01.375 --> 17:02.957
OK, OK. OK.

17:02.958 --> 17:05.416
Spirit, come on.
Police up your shit.

17:05.417 --> 17:07.958
All right,
Tiny says fun's over.

17:11.958 --> 17:14.417
[atmospheric music builds]

17:22.833 --> 17:25.417
Brisbane. Beautiful.

17:30.958 --> 17:33.083
And a river runs through it.

17:34.958 --> 17:37.874
[unsettling music]

17:37.875 --> 17:40.624
[Ben] OK, you still haven't
answered the question.

17:40.625 --> 17:42.457
Are you a Francophile?

17:42.458 --> 17:44.332
Why do you keep asking me that?

17:44.333 --> 17:47.082
[Ben] You know, you're learning
French, which is unusual,

17:47.083 --> 17:48.707
'cause you're in Australia.

17:48.708 --> 17:50.707
It's like you're Napoleon, right?

17:50.708 --> 17:52.166
Except a big Napoleon!

17:52.167 --> 17:53.791
There's a little girl
in the visor.

17:53.792 --> 17:55.874
Does she have something
to do with it?

17:55.875 --> 17:58.332
- Enough. Mr Bishop--
- "Ben". Call me "Ben".

17:58.333 --> 18:01.749
No... No, <i>Mr Bishop!</i>
Look, I don't know you, OK?

18:01.750 --> 18:03.457
And to be completely honest,
I--

18:03.458 --> 18:05.999
[unsettling music builds]

18:06.000 --> 18:07.624
Oh, shit.

18:07.625 --> 18:08.749
What's the matter?

18:08.750 --> 18:10.625
[tires screeching]

18:25.083 --> 18:26.957
Let me ask you a question.

18:26.958 --> 18:28.999
How much does one of those
go for on the black market?

18:29.000 --> 18:30.707
Why would you ask me
something like that?

18:30.708 --> 18:32.292
Just answer the question.

18:32.958 --> 18:34.582
Well, if someone's
desperate enough

18:34.583 --> 18:36.249
and they got the money...

18:36.250 --> 18:39.082
For this particular liver?
I dunno, a million, maybe.

18:39.083 --> 18:41.041
- A million?
- Well, I mean... [stammering]

18:41.042 --> 18:42.666
The donor and recipient

18:42.667 --> 18:45.041
have the rarest blood type
on the planet.

18:45.042 --> 18:47.124
Rh-null.
People call it "golden blood".

18:47.125 --> 18:49.457
So if you only got 50 or 60
people in the world

18:49.458 --> 18:52.249
walking around with it,
it's kinda priceless.

18:52.250 --> 18:54.791
But, Hank, I really don't like
this conversation.

18:54.792 --> 18:56.417
Where are you going with this?

18:58.000 --> 18:59.458
OK.

19:04.625 --> 19:06.374
Do you know how the donor died?

19:06.375 --> 19:08.332
No. And I'm asking you,
where are you going--

19:08.333 --> 19:11.166
- Just answer the question.
- I...

19:11.167 --> 19:14.875
I can look on the online
database - Godspeed.

19:20.292 --> 19:21.417
What?

19:22.833 --> 19:24.417
Homicide.

19:29.333 --> 19:31.416
Don't turn around at what
I'm about to tell you.

19:31.417 --> 19:33.457
- What?
- I believe the same group

19:33.458 --> 19:35.749
that killed that guy in Hawaii
is following us now.

19:35.750 --> 19:37.207
What are you talking about?

19:37.208 --> 19:40.541
I need you to listen to me,
Ben. Do exactly as I say.

19:40.542 --> 19:42.166
- Hold it--
- [Hank] Take your phone out,

19:42.167 --> 19:44.207
get the camera up,
reverse the lens.

19:44.208 --> 19:45.999
Soon as that car behind us
gets close enough,

19:46.000 --> 19:47.832
I want you to take a picture
of the license plate.

19:47.833 --> 19:49.374
- You understand?
- W...

19:49.375 --> 19:51.457
I'm gonna take us
on a little detour downtown.

19:51.458 --> 19:53.208
[engine revs]

19:55.042 --> 19:58.708
[tense music builds]

20:01.042 --> 20:03.124
OK, it's behind us.

20:03.125 --> 20:04.708
I see it.

20:09.208 --> 20:10.458
[tires screeching]

20:11.750 --> 20:14.416
Are you seeing this? There's
a second car right behind us.

20:14.417 --> 20:16.166
Calm down. I see it.

20:16.167 --> 20:17.916
[tires screeching]

20:17.917 --> 20:20.542
- [tense music continues]
- [tires screech]

20:28.000 --> 20:29.999
Good - they didn't make
the turn, it's just the one.

20:30.000 --> 20:31.957
[tense music builds]

20:31.958 --> 20:33.916
[driver] Hey, buddy!
I'm talking to you!

20:33.917 --> 20:35.791
What are you doing? Come on,
I gotta get outta here!

20:35.792 --> 20:37.791
- You can't stop there!
- [horns blaring]

20:37.792 --> 20:40.167
- [Ben] Hey, what's he doing?
- Snap the plate.

20:41.042 --> 20:42.832
- [cell phone clicks]
- I got it.

20:42.833 --> 20:44.582
[Hank] Here we go.

20:44.583 --> 20:46.625
- [horns blaring]
- [tires screeching]

20:51.000 --> 20:53.166
That got the heart goin'.

20:53.167 --> 20:56.541
No more jet lag,
I tell ya that. I'm wide awake.

20:56.542 --> 20:58.916
Turns out fear
gets rid of jet lag.

20:58.917 --> 21:00.832
[tires screeching]

21:00.833 --> 21:02.875
[ominous sting]

21:05.292 --> 21:07.625
Hey... what do we do?

21:09.417 --> 21:10.874
Stay calm.

21:10.875 --> 21:14.792
[ominous music builds]

21:26.542 --> 21:28.374
Are you seeing what I'm seeing?

21:28.375 --> 21:30.166
[Hank] I see them.

21:30.167 --> 21:32.624
Guns. They got guns.

21:32.625 --> 21:34.792
[Hank] Stay calm.

21:35.750 --> 21:37.457
- Stay calm?
- That's right.

21:37.458 --> 21:40.374
[Ben] That's what they say
right before the plane's about

21:40.375 --> 21:42.249
to crash - which really means,
"Pray."

21:42.250 --> 21:44.041
Which really means,
"We're fucked!"

21:44.042 --> 21:45.874
Yeah, 'cause I'm not
getting calming energy

21:45.875 --> 21:48.166
from the Grim Reaper there
or this guy.

21:48.167 --> 21:51.332
Ben. Keep your hand
on the package.

21:51.333 --> 21:53.207
Secure the bird if you can.

21:53.208 --> 21:54.667
What?

21:56.250 --> 21:57.624
[engine revs sharply]

21:57.625 --> 21:58.792
[biker grunts]

22:00.083 --> 22:01.374
- [grunts]
- [glass shatters]

22:01.375 --> 22:03.416
- [gunshots ring out]
- Go, go, go!

22:03.417 --> 22:05.124
- [bird] Peekaboo!
- [pedestrians shouting]

22:05.125 --> 22:07.208
[gunshots ring out]

22:08.208 --> 22:09.916
[man in suit]
Let's go! Come on!

22:09.917 --> 22:13.041
[dramatic music rises]

22:13.042 --> 22:15.166
- [music subsides]
- Hey, Julie.

22:15.167 --> 22:16.916
Hey. Hey.

22:16.917 --> 22:19.874
When is the guy
gonna call, again?

22:19.875 --> 22:23.124
Dr Ainsley said the courier
checks in at the halfway mark.

22:23.125 --> 22:25.124
And how long from now is that?

22:25.125 --> 22:26.916
I've checked my phone
so many times

22:26.917 --> 22:28.957
I don't even know what the hell
I'm looking at anymore.

22:28.958 --> 22:32.249
We're tracking it, Kate. OK?
I'm sorry.

22:32.250 --> 22:35.124
But we will let you know
as soon as we hear anything.

22:35.125 --> 22:36.750
OK? I promise.

22:38.333 --> 22:40.917
[dramatic music swells]

22:44.250 --> 22:45.957
From the time that liver
stepped out of a body

22:45.958 --> 22:47.374
to the time it stepped
into this car,

22:47.375 --> 22:48.416
someone got bought off.

22:48.417 --> 22:49.707
How many people
know what you have

22:49.708 --> 22:50.916
and where you're headed?

22:50.917 --> 22:52.541
I don't know, I...

22:52.542 --> 22:54.707
[Ben breathing unevenly]

22:54.708 --> 22:56.582
You know what?
We gotta pull over.

22:56.583 --> 22:58.374
I gotta go... I'm having
a hard time breathing.

22:58.375 --> 22:59.999
Ben, not a good time
to freak out right now.

23:00.000 --> 23:01.999
I'm not freaking out, but
I want to get out of this car.

23:02.000 --> 23:03.832
No, we can't get out of
the car right now, Ben, OK?

23:03.833 --> 23:05.499
- Take a deep breath.
- OK. Yeah...

23:05.500 --> 23:07.041
All right, I need you
not to freak out.

23:07.042 --> 23:09.374
I'm processing, OK?
I wanna get out of the car.

23:09.375 --> 23:11.374
- You're freaking out right now.
- This is processing.

23:11.375 --> 23:13.499
And processing means, get
the fuck out of the car now!

23:13.500 --> 23:15.624
- [Hank] Oh, shit.
- Now what?

23:15.625 --> 23:18.041
[Hank] Don't worry. Put your
hand on your chest and breathe.

23:18.042 --> 23:19.457
Just think for one second,
OK?

23:19.458 --> 23:21.917
Think through the people
that know. Count.

23:23.042 --> 23:25.374
OK, uh... from the surgeon

23:25.375 --> 23:28.499
to the stewardess
and the pilots, 12.

23:28.500 --> 23:30.916
Or no... with you guys,
I guess, 14.

23:30.917 --> 23:33.707
- Who are the last two?
- You and your employer.

23:33.708 --> 23:35.082
[ominous sting]

23:35.083 --> 23:37.375
[cell phone ringing]

23:38.708 --> 23:39.999
[tires screeching]

23:40.000 --> 23:42.332
Hey. Hey...

23:42.333 --> 23:45.082
You... you know,
maybe this <i>is</i> a one-man job.

23:45.083 --> 23:46.957
You're obviously a capable guy

23:46.958 --> 23:48.541
and I don't want to
slow you down.

23:48.542 --> 23:51.249
I probably oversold
how complicated this is.

23:51.250 --> 23:53.082
- It's a refrigerated cooler.
- [bird] Peekaboo!

23:53.083 --> 23:55.332
You drop it off, you give 'em
the codes, you're done.

23:55.333 --> 23:58.041
Just drop me off up ahead,
I'll figure my own way back.

23:58.042 --> 23:59.832
- [ringing continues]
- [tense music builds]

23:59.833 --> 24:02.833
Did you hear me?
Hey? Are you listening to me?

24:03.750 --> 24:05.499
[Iggy] <i>Didn't I tell you
to pick up your phone?</i>

24:05.500 --> 24:06.874
- Iggy, listen--<i>-No.</i>

24:06.875 --> 24:08.832
<i>Do you have any idea
how pissed off they are?</i>

24:08.833 --> 24:10.874
<i>You've completely
horse-fucked this, Hank!</i>

24:10.875 --> 24:13.124
<i>They want you to pull over
right now and wait for them</i>

24:13.125 --> 24:15.249
<i>- to confirm the address--</i>
- Iggy, shut up and listen, OK?

24:15.250 --> 24:17.207
We got a serious fuckin'
problem here. What?

24:17.208 --> 24:19.707
I don't know who the "they" is
he's referring to.

24:19.708 --> 24:22.291
<i>Hank. Hank!</i>

24:22.292 --> 24:24.791
- [Hank] What do you mean?
- The hospital has <i>my</i> number.

24:24.792 --> 24:26.499
They're waiting for <i>my</i> call,
not <i>his.</i>

24:26.500 --> 24:28.041
Are you sure they
wouldn't call him?

24:28.042 --> 24:29.499
[Ben] No.
They don't have his number.

24:29.500 --> 24:30.999
[Iggy] <i>Hank,
what the fuck, mate?</i>

24:31.000 --> 24:32.999
[Hank] Iggy, I'm gonna call
you back in a second, buddy.

24:33.000 --> 24:34.957
<i>- No. No, you're kidding me--</i>
- [phone beeps]

24:34.958 --> 24:37.916
- Keep going.
- There's no grey area here.

24:37.917 --> 24:40.707
All lines of communication
gotta go through me, legally.

24:40.708 --> 24:43.291
Once the package is in transit,
that's the way it works.

24:43.292 --> 24:45.542
[tense music continues]

24:51.292 --> 24:53.208
- [knocking]
- [Dr Ainsley] <i>Come in.</i>

24:55.333 --> 24:56.374
Hi.

24:56.375 --> 24:58.582
Sorry to bother you, Doctor.

24:58.583 --> 25:01.291
Um, I know there's a protocol
about when the courier calls,

25:01.292 --> 25:03.041
but I was just...

25:03.042 --> 25:05.666
- I... I'm just going--
- Yes, I get it. Mm-hm.

25:05.667 --> 25:08.749
Is... is there any chance
that we can just

25:08.750 --> 25:11.124
call the guy right now
and... and check in?

25:11.125 --> 25:13.124
Just make sure
everything's OK?

25:13.125 --> 25:15.083
It would make me feel
so much better.

25:17.000 --> 25:18.582
Uh... of course. Of course.

25:18.583 --> 25:20.917
Let me just find his number.

25:22.375 --> 25:24.249
[engines revving,
tires screeching]

25:24.250 --> 25:27.207
[dramatic music rises]

25:27.208 --> 25:31.750
[cell phone ringing]

25:34.000 --> 25:35.957
- [Iggy] <i>Hank.</i>
- I'm here, Iggy.

25:35.958 --> 25:37.249
<i>Hank, I swear to God,</i>

25:37.250 --> 25:38.874
<i>if you hang up on me again,
I'm gonna--</i>

25:38.875 --> 25:40.874
You'll what?
You'll fucking what?!

25:40.875 --> 25:43.957
<i>Just pull the car over, Hank!
Just please, please pull over.</i>

25:43.958 --> 25:46.291
- [cell phone ringing]
- You're not a criminal, Iggy.

25:46.292 --> 25:47.832
Are they listening in
right now?

25:47.833 --> 25:49.249
<i>Yes.</i>

25:49.250 --> 25:51.291
<i>And I need you to listen to me.</i>

25:51.292 --> 25:53.332
[voice cracking]<i>Hank... Hank...</i>

25:53.333 --> 25:55.667
[Iggy choking, spluttering]

25:57.042 --> 25:59.125
- [strained] <i>Hank...</i> [choking]
- Iggy?

26:00.917 --> 26:02.167
Iggy?

26:03.042 --> 26:04.416
[man with accent]<i>All you had to do</i>

26:04.417 --> 26:06.666
<i>was roll down your window
and hand me the case.</i>

26:06.667 --> 26:08.582
<i>Never have to see me again.</i>

26:08.583 --> 26:11.374
<i>But it's a new world now,
don't you think,</i>

26:11.375 --> 26:13.167
<i>Hank Malone?</i>

26:14.417 --> 26:16.832
<i>You're ex-military, no?</i>

26:16.833 --> 26:18.916
<i>Big macho American
in the desert?</i>

26:18.917 --> 26:22.500
<i>So you know how quickly
shit can get out of control.</i>

26:23.833 --> 26:26.082
[line ringing]

26:26.083 --> 26:27.916
You're not Australian either, huh?

26:27.917 --> 26:29.999
[man] <i>No shit.
What gave me away?</i>

26:30.000 --> 26:31.374
[Hank] Dumb accent.

26:31.375 --> 26:33.582
The fact that most of the
Aussies I've met are nice.

26:33.583 --> 26:35.249
You sound like an arsehole.

26:35.250 --> 26:37.250
<i>I can be nice, if you can.</i>

26:38.750 --> 26:40.832
We gonna keep flirting
or you gonna tell me the rules

26:40.833 --> 26:42.457
of this "new world"?

26:42.458 --> 26:44.624
[man laughs]<i>Here are the rules.</i>

26:44.625 --> 26:47.374
<i>Pull that Land Cruiser over
and give me what I want,</i>

26:47.375 --> 26:49.333
<i>or I'm going to kill him.</i>

26:53.167 --> 26:56.291
<i>How about we do one of
those classic countdowns?</i>

26:56.292 --> 26:58.207
<i>- What do you think, Iggy?</i>
- [cell phone ringing]

26:58.208 --> 27:00.082
<i>Let's give your little runner
here a chance</i>

27:00.083 --> 27:02.207
<i>to do right by the hand
that feeds him.</i>

27:02.208 --> 27:04.499
Hey, should I get this?

27:04.500 --> 27:06.749
[Iggy] <i>Please, Hank.
I'm begging you mate, please.</i>

27:06.750 --> 27:08.499
- Who's getting it?
- Getting what?

27:08.500 --> 27:09.957
The fucking liver, Ben!

27:09.958 --> 27:12.249
- [man with accent] <i>You ready?</i>
- It's for a kid.

27:12.250 --> 27:14.082
- What?
- [Ben] Yeah. Little girl.

27:14.083 --> 27:15.957
<i>She's seven.
Her name's Ellie Baker.</i>

27:15.958 --> 27:18.457
<i>She's got a rare form
of liver cancer, aggressive,</i>

27:18.458 --> 27:20.041
<i>and it's been accelerating.</i>

27:20.042 --> 27:23.041
[man with accent] <i>I'm gonna
take your silence as a yes?</i>

27:23.042 --> 27:25.707
- How long has she been sick?
- Half her life.

27:25.708 --> 27:27.832
And if she doesn't
get this today, that's it,

27:27.833 --> 27:30.292
she's not gonna make it,
she's gonna die.

27:31.458 --> 27:32.874
[horn blaring]

27:32.875 --> 27:34.625
[man] <i>Three...</i>

27:36.250 --> 27:37.832
I'm sorry, Iggy.

27:37.833 --> 27:39.707
[man] <i>..two...</i>

27:39.708 --> 27:41.374
[dramatic music rises]

27:41.375 --> 27:42.832
[tires screeching]

27:42.833 --> 27:45.582
- Hey! Look out!
- [horns blaring]

27:45.583 --> 27:49.083
- Peekaboo!
- [tires screech]

27:51.708 --> 27:53.125
[tires screech]

27:54.167 --> 27:55.583
[man] <i>..one.</i>

27:56.583 --> 27:57.708
[gunshot]

27:59.917 --> 28:01.625
[man] <i>Here's your</i> jefe.

28:07.125 --> 28:09.666
Are you taking me seriously
now, Hank Malone?

28:09.667 --> 28:12.417
[horns beeping]

28:17.958 --> 28:20.625
- [tires screech]
- [horn blares]

28:36.500 --> 28:38.583
Hey! The fuck you think
you're doin'?!

28:43.125 --> 28:44.167
[in English] Damián...

28:45.375 --> 28:46.582
Get out here, you fuck!

28:46.583 --> 28:47.874
[gunshot]

28:47.875 --> 28:49.083
Damián, <i>por favor...</i>

28:53.375 --> 28:54.833
Damián...

28:58.375 --> 28:59.542
[gunshot]

29:05.708 --> 29:07.541
[in English]
It was rhetorical anyways.

29:07.542 --> 29:08.666
[sniffs sharply]

29:08.667 --> 29:11.875
Get this pile of shit
out of my car.

29:13.000 --> 29:14.042
[exhales heavily]

29:16.125 --> 29:18.250
[tires screeching]

29:26.458 --> 29:28.624
Man, who the hell is this guy?

29:28.625 --> 29:30.666
[Hank] Well, my guess is
he's cartel.

29:30.667 --> 29:32.666
Cartel? A...

29:32.667 --> 29:35.999
As in <i>cartel</i> cartel?
Like Pablo Escobar cartel?

29:36.000 --> 29:38.957
Escobar died 40 years ago,
but, yeah, something similar.

29:38.958 --> 29:41.874
Well, what is the cartel doing
in Queensland Australia?

29:41.875 --> 29:43.291
Oh, I don't know, Ben.

29:43.292 --> 29:44.916
Maybe they heard about
the world-class scuba diving.

29:44.917 --> 29:47.457
- [cell phone ringing]
- OK, here, it's the hospital.

29:47.458 --> 29:48.791
This is Ben Bishop.

29:48.792 --> 29:51.874
Ah. Uh... Mr Bishop,
this is Dr Meredith Ainsley.

29:51.875 --> 29:54.166
I'm the Director here at GCCH.

29:54.167 --> 29:56.082
I have a very anxious mom here
who would--

29:56.083 --> 29:58.541
Sure. Meredith, listen, is the
mom in the room with you?

29:58.542 --> 30:01.041
- She is. Mm-hm.<i>-OK, I'm gonna suggest</i>

30:01.042 --> 30:03.042
maybe you have her
leave the room for this.

30:05.833 --> 30:08.874
Um, OK. Uh, sounds like
everything's in order, Kate.

30:08.875 --> 30:10.832
So if you could just
give me the room?

30:10.833 --> 30:12.999
The courier, his name is Ben.
He sounds very nice...

30:13.000 --> 30:15.166
- You're sure everything is...?
- Absolutely.

30:15.167 --> 30:17.207
We just need to bang out
a few boring clerical things.

30:17.208 --> 30:20.082
- [inhales deeply]
- Why don't you go check in

30:20.083 --> 30:22.166
on everyone's
favourite patient, OK?

30:22.167 --> 30:23.875
[softly] Thank you.

30:24.708 --> 30:26.666
[footsteps receding]

30:26.667 --> 30:28.707
What's happening, Ben?

30:28.708 --> 30:31.249
OK, several men,
we don't know who,

30:31.250 --> 30:35.166
followed us from the airport,
and they want what we have.

30:35.167 --> 30:37.125
They want it - bad.

30:39.083 --> 30:41.207
Hello? Meredith?

30:41.208 --> 30:44.124
Uh, sorry, Ben. Yes, um...

30:44.125 --> 30:45.999
Listen, I have no idea
how they knew

30:46.000 --> 30:48.667
this package was arriving
today, but they did.

30:50.542 --> 30:52.750
[unsettling music builds]

31:01.458 --> 31:03.207
It's him.

31:03.208 --> 31:05.750
[breathing raggedly]

31:41.292 --> 31:43.541
[coughing wheezily]

31:43.542 --> 31:44.916
[doctor] Hello?

31:44.917 --> 31:47.249
Listen to me carefully.

31:47.250 --> 31:50.124
If you let anything happen
to her while I'm gone,

31:50.125 --> 31:52.374
I'll cut your own liver
out of your belly

31:52.375 --> 31:54.082
and feed it to
your children tonight.

31:54.083 --> 31:55.374
Understand?

31:55.375 --> 31:56.833
[doctor] Yes.

31:58.250 --> 32:00.750
- [unsettling music intensifies]
- [engine revving]

32:04.708 --> 32:06.666
OK, and how about
calling the police?

32:06.667 --> 32:07.874
If these guys are cartel,

32:07.875 --> 32:09.291
it means they've hired
local muscle.

32:09.292 --> 32:11.124
Local muscle means Infractores.

32:11.125 --> 32:12.832
Infractores means
they paid off the cops.

32:12.833 --> 32:14.957
- [Ben] Oh, come on...
- I'm the only one we can trust.

32:14.958 --> 32:16.582
Hold it. Wait... [stammers]

32:16.583 --> 32:18.875
Who...
Well, what are "Infractors"?

32:19.958 --> 32:21.999
A gang that'll hang you from
the ceiling by your testicles

32:22.000 --> 32:23.124
if you make 'em happy enough.

32:23.125 --> 32:24.666
Wait, w... Why would you

32:24.667 --> 32:26.082
tell me something like that?!

32:26.083 --> 32:27.457
'Cause you asked, Ben.

32:27.458 --> 32:29.374
Yeah, and you know
I'm on edge right now.

32:29.375 --> 32:31.832
That's TMI! Big-time! OK?

32:31.833 --> 32:35.499
Let me give you page one
of the report on Ben Bishop -

32:35.500 --> 32:38.249
not a hang-from-the-testicles
kinda guy, OK?

32:38.250 --> 32:39.916
So-so, we need a plan.

32:39.917 --> 32:41.707
- You got one?
- I'm working on it.

32:41.708 --> 32:43.791
- We need more than that!
- Are you rushing me right now?

32:43.792 --> 32:45.541
We need to get there, OK?

32:45.542 --> 32:47.124
What do you think
I'm trying to do, Ben?!

32:47.125 --> 32:48.916
- You wanna drive, Ben?
- [Ben] No...

32:48.917 --> 32:50.874
Why don't you grab it,
backseat driver?

32:50.875 --> 32:52.707
Just look at the road.
Here we go.

32:52.708 --> 32:54.666
By all means, come up here
and fucking drive.

32:54.667 --> 32:56.041
Listen, I don't know
how to drive

32:56.042 --> 32:57.416
from the opposite side--

32:57.417 --> 32:59.791
- [metal crunching]
- [tires screech]

32:59.792 --> 33:02.042
- [woman] Oh, my God! What--
- [onlookers gasping]

33:04.958 --> 33:06.917
- Dude, you OK?
- [Ben panting]

33:08.292 --> 33:10.083
Not really, no.

33:12.500 --> 33:14.332
[metal crunches, grinds]

33:14.333 --> 33:15.666
[onlookers exclaiming, gasping]

33:15.667 --> 33:17.291
[woman] Oh, my God!
Look what he did!

33:17.292 --> 33:19.042
Well, you said you wanted
to get out.

33:19.833 --> 33:21.332
[man] He just drove right over!

33:21.333 --> 33:22.916
[onlookers muttering
in disbelief]

33:22.917 --> 33:24.499
[woman] Gotta call an
ambulance!

33:24.500 --> 33:26.666
- This way, Ben.
- [woman] He's got a gun!

33:26.667 --> 33:28.999
- [gunshots ring out]
- Grab and stay down!

33:29.000 --> 33:32.124
- [gunshots ring out]
- [panicked shouting, screaming]

33:32.125 --> 33:34.582
- Agh!
- [gunshots ring out]

33:34.583 --> 33:36.707
- Peekaboo!
- Spirit!

33:36.708 --> 33:38.041
[mouthing silently]

33:38.042 --> 33:39.457
[screaming continues]

33:39.458 --> 33:42.333
[gunfire]

33:43.167 --> 33:44.583
It's at your 5 o'clock.

33:45.542 --> 33:47.082
How sturdy is that case, Ben?

33:47.083 --> 33:49.166
You can knock it around a
little but you can't shoot it!

33:49.167 --> 33:51.625
- [gunshots]
- OK. OK!

33:52.875 --> 33:54.125
I got this.

33:56.000 --> 33:58.250
[singsong voice] Hank Malone!

33:59.500 --> 34:01.916
I think we got off on the...

34:01.917 --> 34:05.374
er... how do you say in
English, er, <i>"pé errado"?</i>

34:05.375 --> 34:07.042
This fuckin' guy...

34:07.917 --> 34:10.082
I think you're trying to say
"wrong foot", amigo!

34:10.083 --> 34:12.667
Wrong foot! Yes.

34:13.583 --> 34:14.666
Fuck.

34:14.667 --> 34:16.832
Let's be on the right foot,
you and me.

34:16.833 --> 34:18.041
[whispers] Back up.

34:18.042 --> 34:19.832
That's preferable, no?

34:19.833 --> 34:22.957
Hey, what do you say we start
with you putting away your gun?

34:22.958 --> 34:25.042
Ooh. Guns down?

34:26.792 --> 34:28.124
OK.

34:28.125 --> 34:31.417
Guns down.

34:33.042 --> 34:35.457
You know, Iggy spoke
so highly of you.

34:35.458 --> 34:37.166
[Hank]
That's really sweet of him.

34:37.167 --> 34:39.082
He called you...

34:39.083 --> 34:41.333
...his gentle giant.

34:42.292 --> 34:45.499
So you must agree, it would
be best if we kept things...

34:45.500 --> 34:47.332
...gentle.

34:47.333 --> 34:49.207
Oh, of course.

34:49.208 --> 34:50.916
[whispers]
What are you doing? Hank!

34:50.917 --> 34:53.208
Why don't we shake on it,
go for a beer?

34:53.917 --> 34:56.042
[laughs]

34:57.750 --> 34:59.749
Why do you even care?

34:59.750 --> 35:02.166
Some bitch you don't know
has a shitty day,

35:02.167 --> 35:03.999
what does it matter to you?

35:04.000 --> 35:06.041
What's it matter to you?

35:06.042 --> 35:07.666
A million?

35:07.667 --> 35:09.707
That sound about right?

35:09.708 --> 35:11.417
You don't know nothing.

35:17.500 --> 35:19.457
Don't make me kill
more innocent people today,

35:19.458 --> 35:21.082
gentle giant.

35:21.083 --> 35:24.167
Oh, no, we don't want anybody
else to die over this.

35:25.917 --> 35:27.624
This case is so much trouble, dude.

35:27.625 --> 35:29.207
- [whispers] Gimme the case.
- What?

35:29.208 --> 35:30.707
- [Hank] Give it.
- No.

35:30.708 --> 35:32.417
- Ben, give it.
- Hey, no.

35:33.042 --> 35:34.917
- [whispers] Goddammit, no!
- Give me the case.

35:36.375 --> 35:37.667
[shouting] All right!

35:38.250 --> 35:39.833
Here it is! See?

35:40.417 --> 35:42.292
I'm gonna leave it right here!

35:42.958 --> 35:45.499
- It's all yours, OK?
- That sounds good.

35:45.500 --> 35:47.292
[Hank] We're gonna
back away slowly...

35:49.250 --> 35:50.917
...so no one gets hurt.

35:53.625 --> 35:57.500
[tense music builds]

35:59.292 --> 36:00.457
[gasps]

36:00.458 --> 36:02.499
- [explosion booms]
- [bikers grunt]

36:02.500 --> 36:04.167
- [fire whooshes]
- [bikers exclaim]

36:10.125 --> 36:11.291
[slow rock music]

36:11.292 --> 36:15.707
<i>♪ You must beware ♪</i>

36:15.708 --> 36:20.249
<i>♪ There's violence in ♪</i>

36:20.250 --> 36:21.541
Go this way.

36:21.542 --> 36:23.374
<i>♪ The air... ♪</i>

36:23.375 --> 36:24.541
Stop.

36:24.542 --> 36:27.124
- [fires gun]
- [woman] He's got a gun!

36:27.125 --> 36:29.166
[panicked shouting, screaming]

36:29.167 --> 36:30.832
Hank!

36:30.833 --> 36:34.917
["Motor City Madhouse" plays]

36:36.125 --> 36:37.250
[cocks gun]

36:39.417 --> 36:40.916
[Ben groans]

36:40.917 --> 36:42.625
[biker] Gimme the fuckin' case.

36:45.917 --> 36:48.042
Tell 'em we got it.
[grunts]

36:48.917 --> 36:50.542
[wails in agony]

36:51.458 --> 36:52.583
[biker groans]

36:53.208 --> 36:55.749
- Stay the fuck down!<i>-♪ Whoa, when you see my name ♪</i>

36:55.750 --> 36:58.416
<i>♪ Gonna set this town a flame
That's right ♪</i>

36:58.417 --> 37:00.125
- [gunshots]
- [biker cries out]

37:01.042 --> 37:02.125
[gunshot]

37:02.958 --> 37:05.541
- [Hank grunts]<i>-♪ Whoa! You best beware ♪</i>

37:05.542 --> 37:07.749
<i>♪ There's violence
in the air tonight ♪</i>

37:07.750 --> 37:09.457
[biker screams]

37:09.458 --> 37:10.749
[biker] Get the fuckin' case!

37:10.750 --> 37:12.374
- [bones crack]<i>-♪ This mad dog town's ♪</i>

37:12.375 --> 37:13.957
<i>♪ Gonna set you free ♪</i>

37:13.958 --> 37:16.875
<i>- ♪ Gonna set you free ♪</i>
- [biker] You son of a bitch!

37:17.833 --> 37:19.167
[groans]

37:20.542 --> 37:22.042
Get the case!

37:23.125 --> 37:24.416
Get the gun!

37:24.417 --> 37:25.874
[gunshot]

37:25.875 --> 37:27.374
[cocks gun]

37:27.375 --> 37:28.792
- [gunshot]
- [biker grunts]

37:29.917 --> 37:31.957
- You mother--!<i>-♪ Whoa... ♪</i>

37:31.958 --> 37:33.082
[gunshot]

37:33.083 --> 37:34.458
[biker screams]

37:37.500 --> 37:39.124
- Agh!<i>-♪ Hey! ♪</i>

37:39.125 --> 37:40.874
<i>♪ Motor City madhouse ♪</i>

37:40.875 --> 37:42.999
<i>- ♪ Motor City madhouse ♪</i>
- [biker groans]

37:43.000 --> 37:47.041
<i>♪ Motor City madhouse ♪</i>

37:47.042 --> 37:49.166
<i>- ♪ Motor City madhouse ♪</i>
- [gunshot]

37:49.167 --> 37:50.957
[biker moans]<i>♪ Motor City madhouse ♪</i>

37:50.958 --> 37:54.791
<i>♪ Motor City madhouse ♪</i>
- You shot my arse!

37:54.792 --> 37:57.041
<i>♪ Motor City madhouse ♪</i>

37:57.042 --> 38:02.167
[song slowing down]<i>♪ Motor City madhouse. ♪</i>

38:04.125 --> 38:06.499
Let me say it for him... Uncle.

38:06.500 --> 38:08.082
Let's go.

38:08.083 --> 38:09.207
[body thuds]

38:09.208 --> 38:11.167
[people screaming]

38:12.125 --> 38:13.999
Hold on, hold on, man.
I gotta get this shit...

38:14.000 --> 38:16.041
- What are ya doin'?
- I gotta get this off.

38:16.042 --> 38:18.624
What are you doing?
You gotta do that right now?

38:18.625 --> 38:20.582
Yeah,
'cause I can't breathe, man.

38:20.583 --> 38:22.041
[vehicle approaching]

38:22.042 --> 38:23.583
[Ben] What? What?

38:24.500 --> 38:26.083
They're somewhere here.

38:28.792 --> 38:29.917
Yeah.

38:31.792 --> 38:33.375
Yeah. This way.

38:35.292 --> 38:37.416
[uneasy music swells]

38:37.417 --> 38:38.916
[engine starting up]

38:38.917 --> 38:40.625
Iggy, you weasel.

38:42.417 --> 38:43.458
Oh!

38:45.417 --> 38:47.625
Oh, fuck yeah. Let's go.

38:52.833 --> 38:53.958
[cell phone pings]

38:55.000 --> 38:57.541
Fuck! He's in a car.

38:57.542 --> 38:59.167
Let's go!

39:00.792 --> 39:02.624
We aren't gonna
make it on foot.

39:02.625 --> 39:04.291
This ain't gonna work.

39:04.292 --> 39:05.833
- [Hank huffs]
- Hey.

39:06.625 --> 39:07.833
Come on.

39:09.750 --> 39:11.666
I know someone who can help.

39:11.667 --> 39:13.541
They're five minutes from here.

39:13.542 --> 39:16.000
[dramatic music]

39:17.042 --> 39:18.833
[tires screech]

39:28.625 --> 39:30.667
[uneasy music]

39:42.917 --> 39:44.416
Where are they?

39:44.417 --> 39:48.332
[driver whimpers, wails]

39:48.333 --> 39:50.374
Where the fuck are they?

39:50.375 --> 39:52.374
I don't know what you're
fucking talking about!

39:52.375 --> 39:54.499
[driver wails]

39:54.500 --> 39:56.125
[frustrated sigh]

40:09.958 --> 40:11.792
[mutters]

40:19.250 --> 40:20.707
Hey.

40:20.708 --> 40:22.499
I know you didn't really
sign up for this,

40:22.500 --> 40:24.332
so if you want to bail,
now's the time.

40:24.333 --> 40:27.207
Bail? Ben Bishop
can't bail now.

40:27.208 --> 40:29.666
Especially not after I've done
all the hard stuff. No way.

40:29.667 --> 40:31.792
We're both heroes today.

40:38.583 --> 40:39.958
[Ben] Knock.

40:40.542 --> 40:41.874
How do I look?

40:41.875 --> 40:43.499
What do you mean?
You look fine.

40:43.500 --> 40:45.166
- You got some blood on you.
- You look crazy.

40:45.167 --> 40:46.957
- Do I look like you?
- Just tuck in your shirt.

40:46.958 --> 40:48.582
Tuck in my shirt?
You're covered in blood!

40:48.583 --> 40:50.417
[woman] Meet you outside!

40:52.667 --> 40:53.957
Hank?

40:53.958 --> 40:55.082
Hi, Mon.

40:55.083 --> 40:56.708
What are you doing here?

40:58.458 --> 40:59.791
Are you leaving?

40:59.792 --> 41:01.916
Yeah, we're just...
we're going for a walk.

41:01.917 --> 41:03.374
OK.

41:03.375 --> 41:04.624
Uh...

41:04.625 --> 41:06.374
Hi.

41:06.375 --> 41:08.416
- Hi. I'm Monica.
- Oh, this is...

41:08.417 --> 41:11.041
- I'm, uh... Hank's ex- wife.
- Hi.

41:11.042 --> 41:12.457
Oh!

41:12.458 --> 41:13.916
OK!

41:13.917 --> 41:16.499
Well, I'm Ben Bishop.
I'm a good friend of Hank's.

41:16.500 --> 41:18.541
And, yeah, we've...
you know, as you can see,

41:18.542 --> 41:20.624
we've got a little bit of
a situation here.

41:20.625 --> 41:23.249
- It's been kind of a crazy...
- Oh!

41:23.250 --> 41:25.417
You're Hank's sponsor?

41:26.083 --> 41:27.916
- Oh, n-no, I'm not his sponsor.
- What? No...

41:27.917 --> 41:30.374
I'm... I'm a little bit of a
mentor, I can see that, but...

41:30.375 --> 41:32.374
No, this has nothing
to do with his recovery.

41:32.375 --> 41:33.582
I've taught him things.

41:33.583 --> 41:36.042
[Josh]
OK, we're strapped and ready!

41:37.042 --> 41:38.666
Hey. Hank?

41:38.667 --> 41:40.124
- How are ya?
- Great, Josh.

41:40.125 --> 41:42.167
- You all right?
- Yeah, I'm fine.

41:43.000 --> 41:45.249
- Ben Bishop. How's it going?
- Hey. How you doing? Josh.

41:45.250 --> 41:48.582
Hi, Josh. And who is
this little wild man?

41:48.583 --> 41:51.582
[Josh] This little ankle biter
is Jack. Say, "Hi," Jack.

41:51.583 --> 41:53.957
- [Ben] Hi. He's so cute!
[Josh] Hi, Jack. Hey.

41:53.958 --> 41:56.416
- Is that a Guaruba guarouba?!
- Yeah.

41:56.417 --> 41:59.249
Wow! They're worth a lot. How'd
ya get your hands on that?

41:59.250 --> 42:01.457
Can someone just tell me
what the hell's going on?

42:01.458 --> 42:03.249
[Spirit caws]

42:03.250 --> 42:04.416
Uh...

42:04.417 --> 42:06.041
Well, I can't explain the bird,

42:06.042 --> 42:08.207
'cause Hank hasn't told me
that part of the story.

42:08.208 --> 42:09.749
Too long to tell, apparently.

42:09.750 --> 42:11.291
But the rest of it's
pretty easy.

42:11.292 --> 42:13.332
There's a little girl
that's very sick

42:13.333 --> 42:15.749
in the Gold Coast
Children's Hospital.

42:15.750 --> 42:18.999
And this guy -
your ex-husband, hero here -

42:19.000 --> 42:22.249
is transporting me
so I can bring her a new liver.

42:22.250 --> 42:23.707
And we need a car.

42:23.708 --> 42:26.082
And also some sunscreen,
if you got it.

42:26.083 --> 42:28.166
Uh, because I left it
in Hank's car,

42:28.167 --> 42:30.708
and that's currently on fire.

42:32.708 --> 42:34.083
He blew it up.

42:35.250 --> 42:36.792
It was a diversion.

42:38.000 --> 42:40.082
Right. OK. Um...

42:40.083 --> 42:42.041
Ye... Yes. Yes, of course.

42:42.042 --> 42:44.749
Yes. Oh, fuck, no, sorry.
We don't have a car.

42:44.750 --> 42:46.374
We were literally walking
to go pick it up.

42:46.375 --> 42:48.291
- Where's your car?
- We left it at the concert hall

42:48.292 --> 42:50.041
in Bundall last night
'cause we went to a gig...

42:50.042 --> 42:51.874
- and we weren't gonna drink...
- Had a bit to drink.

42:51.875 --> 42:53.374
- We don't drink and drive.
- That's good.

42:53.375 --> 42:56.207
Anyway... you can go
and pick it up there. OK? Yeah?

42:56.208 --> 42:58.082
- Yeah, I've got the keys on me.
- [Ben] Great.

42:58.083 --> 43:00.416
Here you go. Uh, let me get you
some sunscreen?

43:00.417 --> 43:01.958
- Yeah, thank you.
- Yeah?

43:04.917 --> 43:05.957
[Hank] Er...

43:05.958 --> 43:07.333
[Ben sighs awkwardly]

43:10.667 --> 43:12.375
Crazy world, right?

43:13.292 --> 43:15.292
Oh. I'll give you a second.

43:18.000 --> 43:21.291
[tender atmospheric music]

43:21.292 --> 43:22.457
[chuckles softly]

43:22.458 --> 43:24.332
Can I see the coin?

43:24.333 --> 43:25.583
Oh.

43:26.375 --> 43:27.542
Yeah.

43:28.333 --> 43:29.750
I put it...

43:39.083 --> 43:40.708
Big day.

43:41.958 --> 43:43.457
Big year.

43:43.458 --> 43:46.125
[tender music continues]

43:48.833 --> 43:50.416
She would have...

43:50.417 --> 43:52.458
She would have been
so proud of you.

43:54.625 --> 43:56.250
Yeah, I hope so.

43:59.042 --> 44:00.625
[Josh] Found it!

44:01.250 --> 44:03.332
[Ben] Oh, great.
Thank you, Josh.

44:03.333 --> 44:05.041
- And thank you, Monica.
- Here you go.

44:05.042 --> 44:06.707
And, most of all,
thank you, Jack.

44:06.708 --> 44:09.958
And who knows? Maybe
we'll have dinner one day.

44:10.625 --> 44:12.750
OK. We gotta move.

44:13.542 --> 44:16.499
Oh, hey, uh... look, this
bird's worth a small fortune.

44:16.500 --> 44:18.792
Maybe it'd be good
for Jack's college fund.

44:19.833 --> 44:21.624
Ah... I don't know
what to say.

44:21.625 --> 44:23.207
You don't have to
say anything.

44:23.208 --> 44:25.000
Hey, look at this.

44:25.792 --> 44:26.957
Peekaboo!

44:26.958 --> 44:29.041
[laughs] It gets me every time!

44:29.042 --> 44:31.416
It's incredible.
He goes by "Spirit".

44:31.417 --> 44:33.457
Guys, the car's the
yellow Kia. You can't miss it.

44:33.458 --> 44:35.124
Concert Hall's
a bit of a hike, though.

44:35.125 --> 44:36.499
- What do you mean, a hike?
- A hike?

44:36.500 --> 44:38.582
- I mean, it's a long walk.
How long?

44:38.583 --> 44:42.541
You know what?
Don't worry. I gotcha.

44:42.542 --> 44:44.167
[footsteps receding]

44:44.917 --> 44:47.667
[puffing]

44:48.375 --> 44:49.791
[Kate] <i>So just to recap...</i>

44:49.792 --> 44:55.082
It can travel through sky, land
and in the ocean.

44:55.083 --> 45:01.000
It has wings, but it's not a
flying monkey with fish gills.

45:02.292 --> 45:03.832
And it's this big.

45:03.833 --> 45:05.542
[respirator hissing steadily]

45:06.875 --> 45:08.082
Hmm.

45:08.083 --> 45:10.124
[weakly] You only have one more

45:10.125 --> 45:12.583
before you have to guess.

45:13.958 --> 45:15.374
[exhales heavily]

45:15.375 --> 45:17.250
Is it real or imaginary?

45:18.000 --> 45:20.708
I... don't... know.

45:21.583 --> 45:24.167
Wow, you've really
stumped Mommy again.

45:25.958 --> 45:27.708
[whispers] Can you tell me?

45:28.292 --> 45:30.625
An angel.

45:31.417 --> 45:33.207
[gentle ethereal vocalising]

45:33.208 --> 45:38.292
[alarm beeping rapidly]

45:39.375 --> 45:41.124
- [bell rings]
- Help!

45:41.125 --> 45:42.249
Someone!

45:42.250 --> 45:45.207
[rapid beeping continues]

45:45.208 --> 45:47.624
She just started bleeding.

45:47.625 --> 45:48.999
What's happening?

45:49.000 --> 45:50.416
Tell me what's happening!

45:50.417 --> 45:52.207
[nurse] We need to
move her to the ICU.

45:52.208 --> 45:54.249
- [uneasy music swells]
- [PA announcer] <i>A code blue.</i>

45:54.250 --> 45:56.082
<i>Dr Ainsley to ICU.</i>

45:56.083 --> 45:57.832
<i>Repeat - code blue...</i>

45:57.833 --> 46:00.332
- Is she gonna die?
- She's stable for the moment.

46:00.333 --> 46:03.542
[intense music builds]

46:09.542 --> 46:11.541
- Kate.
- Julie, what are you doing?

46:11.542 --> 46:13.749
Come in. Shut the door.

46:13.750 --> 46:16.374
I know this looks
incredibly unprofessional,

46:16.375 --> 46:19.124
but after Ainsley
spoke with the courier,

46:19.125 --> 46:22.707
I overheard her having a heated
conversation with someone.

46:22.708 --> 46:25.374
I don't know, it was like
crazy heated, Kate.

46:25.375 --> 46:27.874
So I came in here to ask her
about it, but she was gone,

46:27.875 --> 46:31.291
I let myself in, and I was
sort of thinking about...

46:31.292 --> 46:32.792
Thinking about what?

46:33.500 --> 46:35.499
Searching her computer
for the courier's number

46:35.500 --> 46:37.417
- and calling him myself.
- Yes. Let's do it.

46:38.042 --> 46:39.624
[Hank] I feel you
looking at me.

46:39.625 --> 46:42.791
Well, no... I mean, you know,
the Hank Malone puzzle

46:42.792 --> 46:45.457
is really starting to come
together, I gotta tell ya.

46:45.458 --> 46:47.082
[Hank] You enjoyed that, huh?

46:47.083 --> 46:49.374
[Ben] Well, what wasn't
to enjoy? They're incredible.

46:49.375 --> 46:51.666
I mean, Josh,
what a terrific guy.

46:51.667 --> 46:53.082
[Hank] Josh is a phoney.

46:53.083 --> 46:56.541
[Ben] Oh, come on, he's great,
funny, polite, he's...

46:56.542 --> 46:57.791
If that's being a phoney,

46:57.792 --> 46:59.499
you should try
being more of a phoney!

46:59.500 --> 47:01.749
Oh, so this is what
bucket two feels like.

47:01.750 --> 47:03.541
[laughs] Yeah.

47:03.542 --> 47:05.667
- [cell phone ringing]
- Wait, phone, phone!

47:06.417 --> 47:08.166
He's a handsome guy, too.

47:08.167 --> 47:10.291
[Hank] Traitor.

47:10.292 --> 47:12.541
Huh. Hello?

47:12.542 --> 47:14.374
[Kate] <i>Is this Ben Bishop,
the medical courier?</i>

47:14.375 --> 47:16.124
Ben, we gotta walk and talk.

47:16.125 --> 47:17.791
Yeah. I'm sorry, who is this?

47:17.792 --> 47:20.374
My name is Kate Baker.
I'm the mother.

47:20.375 --> 47:21.791
And I'm freaking out,

47:21.792 --> 47:23.666
and I just need to know
if something's gone wrong.

47:23.667 --> 47:25.541
How did you get this number,
Kate?

47:25.542 --> 47:27.332
<i>Just tell me if something's
gone wrong!</i>

47:27.333 --> 47:28.832
No, no, I-I... Listen.

47:28.833 --> 47:31.457
I understand your concern,
Kate. But is the doctor there?

47:31.458 --> 47:33.374
Because there's a protocol
and I'm only authorised

47:33.375 --> 47:34.999
<i>- to speak with the surgeon...</i>
- Kate!

47:35.000 --> 47:36.832
<i>- ...in charge of the procedure.</i>
- Um, sorry.

47:36.833 --> 47:38.416
Julie?

47:38.417 --> 47:39.832
- [Ben] <i>Hello?</i>
- Who are you talking to?

47:39.833 --> 47:41.082
[Kate] <i>No, no!</i>

47:41.083 --> 47:43.207
Not until someone
gets honest with me!

47:43.208 --> 47:45.458
Ben, you're on speaker.
Start talking.

47:48.625 --> 47:52.375
[sighs] Uh, Ben,
this is Dr Ainsley. Go ahead.

47:53.000 --> 47:55.292
OK, listen.... [stammering]

47:55.875 --> 47:58.124
We had some...
There were some bad people.

47:58.125 --> 48:01.707
<i>We don't know who they were,
but they were pursuing us.</i>

48:01.708 --> 48:03.666
Pursuing you? What do you mean?

48:03.667 --> 48:05.666
They want what we have.

48:05.667 --> 48:07.624
Kate, your daughter
has golden blood,

48:07.625 --> 48:09.916
and, of course,
on the black market,

48:09.917 --> 48:12.041
<i>- that makes this liver very...</i>
- Oh, Jesus Christ.

48:12.042 --> 48:14.207
<i>...you know, valuable
to people who need it.</i>

48:14.208 --> 48:15.624
[Hank] Give me that.

48:15.625 --> 48:17.541
Kate, this is Hank Malone,
I'm Ben's driver

48:17.542 --> 48:19.499
and the man you need
to put your trust in right now.

48:19.500 --> 48:21.291
<i>Listen, I know how
scared you are.</i>

48:21.292 --> 48:22.916
<i>But I also need you
to know this.</i>

48:22.917 --> 48:25.957
I am not a man that people
successfully fuck with.

48:25.958 --> 48:28.417
- OK?
- I can vouch for that.

48:29.792 --> 48:31.582
Listen, there's nothing
in the world that's gonna

48:31.583 --> 48:33.958
keep us from getting to you,
do you understand?

48:35.042 --> 48:37.124
- I do.<i>-OK, good.</i>

48:37.125 --> 48:39.582
<i>Listen, we're picking up a car
at a concert hall in Bundall.</i>

48:39.583 --> 48:40.957
<i>Then we're heading
straight to you.</i>

48:40.958 --> 48:42.957
We'll be there in 40 minutes.

48:42.958 --> 48:45.000
<i>- I'll be at this number.</i>
- [phone beeps]

48:46.042 --> 48:49.166
Kate, I-I... I'm sorry that I
wasn't transparent with you.

48:49.167 --> 48:51.457
I didn't want to frighten you
any more than you already are,

48:51.458 --> 48:55.166
and they had assured me that
everything was under control.

48:55.167 --> 48:56.791
Yeah, well, Julie said
that she overheard you

48:56.792 --> 48:58.666
arguing with someone
on the phone

48:58.667 --> 49:00.583
right after you spoke with Ben.

49:01.333 --> 49:03.708
Uh, what are you
asking me, exactly?

49:05.958 --> 49:07.582
Ah.

49:07.583 --> 49:09.082
Right. Right.

49:09.083 --> 49:12.082
Well, if you must know, I was
speaking with the Director

49:12.083 --> 49:14.291
of the International
Transplant Database,

49:14.292 --> 49:18.374
asking him how in the world
this situation

49:18.375 --> 49:21.208
was even possible
to begin with.

49:22.500 --> 49:24.875
And did I raise
my voice a little?

49:26.417 --> 49:28.416
You're goddamn right I did.

49:28.417 --> 49:31.666
I forgot I grabbed this
after we got T-boned twice.

49:31.667 --> 49:33.749
Figured you'd want it.

49:33.750 --> 49:36.332
The final piece of the puzzle.

49:36.333 --> 49:38.707
- Can I see it?
- You already did.

49:38.708 --> 49:42.207
I barely got to look at it -
we were getting shot at!

49:42.208 --> 49:44.417
Come on. Let me see it.

49:46.583 --> 49:48.749
Are you kidding me?
What a great face.

49:48.750 --> 49:50.624
- Was this a school pic--
- All right, you're done.

49:50.625 --> 49:51.874
Come on, dude...

49:51.875 --> 49:54.624
I'm not asking for
a Shakespearean monologue,

49:54.625 --> 49:56.374
just give me the Hank version.

49:56.375 --> 49:57.707
Why do you care?

49:57.708 --> 50:00.707
Because I'm curious.
I like you.

50:00.708 --> 50:02.582
And I'll probably never
see you again.

50:02.583 --> 50:04.499
It'd be nice to know
something other than,

50:04.500 --> 50:07.625
you know, "brooding
drives fast punchy guy".

50:15.292 --> 50:18.041
Monica and I met
on a military base in Germany.

50:18.042 --> 50:20.416
Fell in love. Had a kid.

50:20.417 --> 50:22.874
I got deployed to Afghanistan.

50:22.875 --> 50:25.083
Did a lot of things
I don't like remembering.

50:26.333 --> 50:28.500
When I came back,
I was a drunk piece of shit.

50:29.667 --> 50:32.458
My daughter Isabel
got sick with leukaemia.

50:33.625 --> 50:35.292
I was a no-show.

50:36.500 --> 50:38.542
I was even drunk
the day she died.

50:45.208 --> 50:46.999
I followed Monica back here.

50:47.000 --> 50:50.500
Tried to make it work.
Failed miserably, obviously.

50:51.708 --> 50:52.791
The end.

50:52.792 --> 50:55.582
Yeah, so now the mission
is stay sober

50:55.583 --> 50:58.666
and do all the cool stuff
Isabel loved,

50:58.667 --> 51:00.832
'cause obviously <i>she's</i>
the Francophile.

51:00.833 --> 51:04.792
Ever since watching that
movie about a rat chef...

51:05.583 --> 51:09.708
...she started wearing berets,
cooking French food.

51:11.000 --> 51:13.041
We were supposed to take a
father/daughter trip to Paris,

51:13.042 --> 51:14.333
but...

51:15.583 --> 51:17.125
...you know...

51:24.917 --> 51:26.375
There it is.

51:27.458 --> 51:29.041
[engine revving]

51:29.042 --> 51:30.499
[tires screech]

51:30.500 --> 51:32.249
[tense music builds]

51:32.250 --> 51:34.958
[tires screech]

51:41.167 --> 51:43.416
[dispatcher on phone] <i>Triple
zero, what is your emergency?</i>

51:43.417 --> 51:44.832
[in English]
No more flirting.

51:44.833 --> 51:47.791
How'd you find us?
I got rid of my phone.

51:47.792 --> 51:50.083
Well, I have eyes
in the whole fucking town.

51:50.708 --> 51:51.957
[Hank groans]

51:51.958 --> 51:53.374
Hey, hey, come on!

51:53.375 --> 51:55.125
[Ben groans]

51:56.208 --> 51:57.457
[moans]

51:57.458 --> 51:59.457
Don't move a muscle, peewee.

51:59.458 --> 52:00.917
[Hank and Ben groan]

52:02.708 --> 52:04.457
[keypad beeps]

52:04.458 --> 52:06.375
[automated female voice]<i>Access denied.</i>

52:09.542 --> 52:10.541
[in English] You OK?

52:10.542 --> 52:13.541
Well, I've had better days.

52:13.542 --> 52:16.541
I thought I'd be having some
oysters and a crisp Chardonnay

52:16.542 --> 52:18.750
with a pretty lady right now,
so...

52:19.667 --> 52:21.416
[chuckles]

52:21.417 --> 52:24.292
<i>Yo también.</i>
We share in this feeling.

52:25.500 --> 52:27.125
Better days indeed.

52:28.083 --> 52:29.624
So I will make things clear,

52:29.625 --> 52:31.999
and maybe you get your oysters.

52:32.000 --> 52:33.457
Huh?

52:33.458 --> 52:35.916
Me and my family,
we run shit here now.

52:35.917 --> 52:37.749
So...

52:37.750 --> 52:39.832
the code...

52:39.833 --> 52:41.167
<i>por favor.</i>

52:49.625 --> 52:50.708
No.

52:52.542 --> 52:53.624
No?

52:53.625 --> 52:55.292
I can't.

52:58.250 --> 53:00.332
Count from three, motherfucker!

53:00.333 --> 53:02.042
[in Spanish]

53:02.667 --> 53:03.957
Ben, don't do it!

53:03.958 --> 53:05.499
- Shut up! Three...
- Don't listen to him.

53:05.500 --> 53:06.791
- Let him shoot me.
- No!

53:06.792 --> 53:08.582
- Just shoot me! Shoot me!
- Two...

53:08.583 --> 53:10.000
- One!
- Wait!

53:11.667 --> 53:13.582
[sirens approaching]

53:13.583 --> 53:15.083
Fuck!

53:15.750 --> 53:17.667
Someone must have called them.

53:18.375 --> 53:20.207
The little one comes with us.

53:20.208 --> 53:23.374
Deal with the cop, hang this
motherfucker from a bridge.

53:23.375 --> 53:25.375
[officer, over megaphone]
Put your guns down!

53:26.375 --> 53:28.625
[gunshots ring out]

53:30.958 --> 53:32.874
Too bad I won't be here
to celebrate my birthday

53:32.875 --> 53:34.457
with you on Monday!

53:34.458 --> 53:36.207
It's my 60th!

53:36.208 --> 53:37.832
Godspeed, big man!

53:37.833 --> 53:40.374
- [biker] Let go, let's go!
- [Ben] Godspeed!

53:40.375 --> 53:42.000
[tires screech]

53:46.125 --> 53:47.957
This isn't how this ends.

53:47.958 --> 53:49.582
[dramatic music swells]

53:49.583 --> 53:51.624
[biker shouts]

53:51.625 --> 53:54.499
OK, all right.
Hang me on the bridge.

53:54.500 --> 53:57.041
- Ah...
- You're damn right we will.

53:57.042 --> 53:58.499
- OK...
- Move!

53:58.500 --> 54:01.541
All right, all right.
I'm cool, I'm going. I'm going.

54:01.542 --> 54:02.791
[biker] Move.

54:02.792 --> 54:04.083
[Hank winces]

54:05.208 --> 54:06.667
[engine starts up]

54:07.792 --> 54:09.707
- [thudding, pounding]
- [grunting]

54:09.708 --> 54:11.958
[gunshots ring out,
glass shatters]

54:14.667 --> 54:16.375
[Hank grunts]

54:17.667 --> 54:18.875
[groans]

54:23.125 --> 54:25.625
Godspeed. Godspeed.

54:26.750 --> 54:28.207
OK...

54:28.208 --> 54:29.583
[cell phone buzzes]

54:30.333 --> 54:32.707
60th birthday... Yeah.

54:32.708 --> 54:35.249
2026...1960... April...

54:35.250 --> 54:38.874
April 11th, 04... 11, 1960...

54:38.875 --> 54:40.417
[puffing]

54:45.000 --> 54:46.957
[exciting music swells]

54:46.958 --> 54:49.750
Ben, you brilliant, beautiful,
annoying man.

54:50.917 --> 54:52.583
We gotta work on
your passwords.

54:56.833 --> 54:59.542
[siren wailing]

55:12.333 --> 55:14.166
[line ringing]

55:14.167 --> 55:15.999
[Detective Manoa]<i>CIB, Detective Manoa.</i>

55:16.000 --> 55:17.666
Hey, Detective,
it's Hank Malone.

55:17.667 --> 55:19.041
I work with Iggy.

55:19.042 --> 55:20.457
He said you could
help me with something.

55:20.458 --> 55:23.291
<i>Ah, Iggy's big American.
What do you need?</i>

55:23.292 --> 55:25.124
- Run a plate for me?<i>-Sure.</i>

55:25.125 --> 55:26.749
- You ready?<i>-Fire away.</i>

55:26.750 --> 55:29.500
Kilo, three, Bravo,
Romeo, one, five.

55:30.583 --> 55:33.957
<i>Wait, K3BR15?</i>

55:33.958 --> 55:35.582
[Hank] Uh, I think that's it.

55:35.583 --> 55:37.582
<i>- Well, I'll be damned.</i>
- What?

55:37.583 --> 55:39.457
<i>This is registered to an
address we've been trying</i>

55:39.458 --> 55:41.166
<i>to get a warrant to
for months.</i>

55:41.167 --> 55:43.541
<i>We think it's an outpost
for Donna Zaldívar.</i>

55:43.542 --> 55:46.291
<i>- You know the name?</i>
- I do not. Who is she?

55:46.292 --> 55:49.041
<i>Mate, she runs the biggest
drug cartel in Colombia.</i>

55:49.042 --> 55:51.417
<i>They control the entire
drug trade down here.</i>

55:52.000 --> 55:53.249
Does she have a son?

55:53.250 --> 55:55.332
<i>Yeah. Damián Zaldívar.</i>

55:55.333 --> 55:58.166
<i>He's a crazy fucker. Might be
even worse than his mother.</i>

55:58.167 --> 56:00.374
<i>You tell Iggy to be careful
with this one.</i>

56:00.375 --> 56:01.791
Right.

56:01.792 --> 56:03.542
Appreciate it, Detective.

56:18.458 --> 56:19.792
Get out.

56:24.125 --> 56:25.541
Go clean up the mess,

56:25.542 --> 56:27.957
and make sure our faces aren't
all over the news tonight.

56:27.958 --> 56:29.292
I'll sort it out.

56:32.208 --> 56:33.457
Let's go.

56:33.458 --> 56:35.916
[unsettling music builds]

56:35.917 --> 56:38.374
Oi. Greedy.

56:38.375 --> 56:40.833
You're with me. Let's go.

56:44.083 --> 56:45.750
All right, boys, shut it down.

56:49.875 --> 56:51.250
[in Spanish]

57:00.667 --> 57:02.458
This is for your mother?

57:03.375 --> 57:05.333
It's not always about money.

57:08.042 --> 57:09.833
Can I have the code now?

57:13.417 --> 57:14.958
Please.

57:16.042 --> 57:18.542
You see, there's a mother<i>I</i> gotta think about.

57:19.500 --> 57:21.582
[unsettling music builds]

57:21.583 --> 57:24.417
I see. Mmm.

57:26.458 --> 57:28.292
Well, let's think about it
over there.

57:30.083 --> 57:31.208
[metal reverberates]

57:38.500 --> 57:39.707
[Ben breathing heavily]

57:39.708 --> 57:41.333
I mean...

57:43.292 --> 57:45.208
[Ben breathes heavily]

57:46.250 --> 57:47.500
[snipping]

57:49.917 --> 57:51.291
Shall we begin?

57:51.292 --> 57:52.832
[quietly] No...

57:52.833 --> 57:54.457
You tell me.

57:54.458 --> 57:56.083
[laboured breathing] I...

57:57.833 --> 57:59.166
- [crash!]
- [Damián exclaims]

57:59.167 --> 58:01.375
[siren wails]

58:02.042 --> 58:03.541
Secure the gate!

58:03.542 --> 58:08.082
[slow rock music]<i>♪ When I'm enraged ♪</i>

58:08.083 --> 58:10.791
<i>♪ Adrenaline rushing ♪</i>

58:10.792 --> 58:16.333
<i>♪ Through my veins... ♪</i>

58:17.625 --> 58:20.125
<i>♪ Baby! ♪</i>
[heavy guitar riff plays]

58:21.750 --> 58:24.582
<i>- ♪ Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah! ♪</i>
- [biker] What the fuck?!

58:24.583 --> 58:25.624
[cocks gun]

58:25.625 --> 58:27.041
That's my ride!

58:27.042 --> 58:28.499
[biker] Oi!

58:28.500 --> 58:30.832
<i>♪ Say I got trouble
Trouble in my eyes ♪</i>

58:30.833 --> 58:32.291
- [bikers grunting]
- Machete!

58:32.292 --> 58:34.124
<i>♪ I'm just looking
for another good time ♪</i>

58:34.125 --> 58:36.041
- [both grunting]<i>-♪ My heart, my heart ♪</i>

58:36.042 --> 58:37.707
<i>♪ Kickstart my heart ♪</i>

58:37.708 --> 58:39.082
[biker groans]

58:39.083 --> 58:40.624
<i>♪ Oh! ♪</i>

58:40.625 --> 58:41.916
<i>♪ Yeah! ♪</i>

58:41.917 --> 58:44.832
<i>♪ Kickstart my heart
Give it a start ♪</i>

58:44.833 --> 58:46.041
<i>- ♪ Oh! ♪</i>
- [gunfire]

58:46.042 --> 58:47.416
<i>♪ Yeah! ♪</i>

58:47.417 --> 58:48.957
Arghh!

58:48.958 --> 58:50.416
- [biker grunts]<i>-♪ Yeah! ♪</i>

58:50.417 --> 58:52.957
- [Hank] You OK?
- [Ben] No!

58:52.958 --> 58:55.582
<i>- ♪ Kickstart my heart... ♪</i>
- Hey! Can you get these off?

58:55.583 --> 58:57.499
I'm workin' on it.

58:57.500 --> 59:00.624
- [Ben grunts]<i>-♪ Baby! ♪</i>

59:00.625 --> 59:01.707
[biker yelling]

59:01.708 --> 59:04.082
OK, next time you ask me
if I wanna bail,

59:04.083 --> 59:06.416
the answer is a yes,
it's "hell yes!"

59:06.417 --> 59:08.207
[gunfire]

59:08.208 --> 59:10.082
- [biker] Where the ammo?
- I offered.

59:10.083 --> 59:11.874
[cocks gun]

59:11.875 --> 59:13.249
<i>♪ Oh! ♪</i>

59:13.250 --> 59:14.791
<i>- ♪ Yeah! ♪</i>
- [Donna] Damián!

59:14.792 --> 59:16.166
<i>♪ Kickstart my heart ♪</i>

59:16.167 --> 59:17.707
<i>♪ Hope it never stops ♪</i>

59:17.708 --> 59:18.999
<i>♪ Oh! ♪</i>

59:19.000 --> 59:20.291
Get the case!

59:20.292 --> 59:22.500
[guns firing]

59:23.500 --> 59:25.332
- [gunshot booms]
- [biker yelps]

59:25.333 --> 59:27.916
[shooting and commotion
continue]

59:27.917 --> 59:29.583
[in Spanish]

59:33.792 --> 59:35.167
[gunshots continue]

59:35.958 --> 59:38.374
It's rush hour - we're gonna
have to double-time it.

59:38.375 --> 59:39.791
Ben, are you gonna help at all?

59:39.792 --> 59:42.249
Dude, my hands
are literally tied!

59:42.250 --> 59:44.042
Why didn't you say something?

59:45.125 --> 59:46.041
[Ben winces]

59:46.042 --> 59:47.708
[in Spanish]

59:54.958 --> 59:57.166
[song continues]<i>♪ Oh! Yeah! ♪</i>

59:57.167 --> 01:00:00.291
<i>♪ Kickstart my heart
Give it a start ♪</i>

01:00:00.292 --> 01:00:02.499
- [gun cocking]<i>-♪ Oh! Yeah! ♪</i>

01:00:02.500 --> 01:00:03.874
He's got the case!

01:00:03.875 --> 01:00:05.499
<i>♪ Baby! ♪</i>

01:00:05.500 --> 01:00:06.791
<i>♪ Oh! ♪</i>

01:00:06.792 --> 01:00:08.416
<i>- ♪ Yeah! ♪</i>
- [biker panting]

01:00:08.417 --> 01:00:10.624
Now you're helping, Ben.

01:00:10.625 --> 01:00:12.124
- [gun fires]
- [biker grunts]

01:00:12.125 --> 01:00:14.249
[cocks gun]
I gotta go.

01:00:14.250 --> 01:00:15.874
Wait, where are you going?

01:00:15.875 --> 01:00:17.167
Don't die.

01:00:18.167 --> 01:00:19.332
I...

01:00:19.333 --> 01:00:22.250
[straining] I should've bailed!

01:00:26.083 --> 01:00:27.250
[cocks gun]

01:00:30.833 --> 01:00:32.000
[bottles clinking]

01:00:43.375 --> 01:00:45.374
[Hank grunts]

01:00:45.375 --> 01:00:46.792
[biker groans]

01:00:49.750 --> 01:00:51.166
[both grunting]

01:00:51.167 --> 01:00:53.375
[biker screaming]

01:01:01.083 --> 01:01:02.250
[bottles clinking]

01:01:06.167 --> 01:01:09.499
[Damián] I tried to be the
reasonable man! Did I not?

01:01:09.500 --> 01:01:12.582
Didn't I try to be
fucking reasonable?!

01:01:12.583 --> 01:01:14.541
You're almost out of time!

01:01:14.542 --> 01:01:16.624
The liver will be useless.

01:01:16.625 --> 01:01:18.832
What a waste it would be, no?

01:01:18.833 --> 01:01:22.042
All this violence and little
Ellie Baker dies anyway!

01:01:24.000 --> 01:01:25.541
[bottles clinking]

01:01:25.542 --> 01:01:27.082
[Damián] Don't let it
go to waste!

01:01:27.083 --> 01:01:28.667
[in Spanish]

01:01:30.208 --> 01:01:31.666
Oh, I won't.

01:01:31.667 --> 01:01:33.624
- [dramatic music rises]
- [biker wails]

01:01:33.625 --> 01:01:35.208
[bottles smashing]

01:01:36.542 --> 01:01:37.875
[cocks gun]

01:01:46.875 --> 01:01:47.958
[Hank grunts]

01:01:57.250 --> 01:01:59.249
[dramatic music escalates]

01:01:59.250 --> 01:02:01.291
[Damián grunts]

01:02:01.292 --> 01:02:04.000
- [water splashes]
- [music fades]

01:02:10.333 --> 01:02:11.875
[Hank] We gotta move.

01:02:14.917 --> 01:02:16.291
[car lock bleeps]

01:02:16.292 --> 01:02:18.374
I was worried you weren't
gonna figure out the password.

01:02:18.375 --> 01:02:20.791
- [Hank] Why?
- I mean, it's a lot of math.

01:02:20.792 --> 01:02:25.083
[low dramatic music builds]

01:02:25.917 --> 01:02:27.208
[engine revs]

01:02:28.958 --> 01:02:30.374
[gunshots]

01:02:30.375 --> 01:02:31.832
[Ben exclaims]

01:02:31.833 --> 01:02:34.958
[dramatic music intensifies]

01:02:35.917 --> 01:02:37.250
[grunts]

01:02:42.333 --> 01:02:43.875
[dramatic music continues]

01:02:50.417 --> 01:02:53.917
[cell phone ringing]

01:02:54.708 --> 01:02:55.707
Yes, ma'am?

01:02:55.708 --> 01:02:57.291
Turn around.

01:02:57.292 --> 01:02:59.416
[Donna] <i>He's in one of
your Land Rovers.</i>

01:02:59.417 --> 01:03:01.332
<i>He's on his way
to the hospital.</i>

01:03:01.333 --> 01:03:02.374
Yes, ma'am.

01:03:02.375 --> 01:03:05.375
[tires screech]

01:03:08.042 --> 01:03:09.207
[alarm beeps]

01:03:09.208 --> 01:03:11.082
- Oh, that's the last one.
- [alarm beeps]

01:03:11.083 --> 01:03:12.457
[under breath] Oh, shit...

01:03:12.458 --> 01:03:14.374
- Ben, your alarm.
- [Ben moans weakly]

01:03:14.375 --> 01:03:15.667
[Hank] Ben, your alarm.

01:03:16.417 --> 01:03:18.332
- Oh, no, no, no, no, no.
- Did I get shot?

01:03:18.333 --> 01:03:20.707
- Oh, God.
- Man, I think I got shot.

01:03:20.708 --> 01:03:22.541
- Lift your shirt, lean forward.
- What?

01:03:22.542 --> 01:03:24.291
I need to see if it
came through the other side.

01:03:24.292 --> 01:03:25.958
What-- [winces]

01:03:28.208 --> 01:03:29.957
[horn blaring]

01:03:29.958 --> 01:03:31.583
[tires screech]

01:03:32.583 --> 01:03:34.792
[moaning]
Did it go through?

01:03:36.083 --> 01:03:36.999
No.

01:03:37.000 --> 01:03:38.416
That's not good.

01:03:38.417 --> 01:03:39.624
We need to stop the bleeding

01:03:39.625 --> 01:03:40.874
and get you medical assistance.

01:03:40.875 --> 01:03:42.708
- We'll have to pull over.
- Keep driving.

01:03:45.750 --> 01:03:47.457
[biker, radio] <i>Heads up,
they're in one of our Rovers</i>

01:03:47.458 --> 01:03:48.957
and they're headed
to the hospital.

01:03:48.958 --> 01:03:50.582
We can't let them
beat us there.

01:03:50.583 --> 01:03:52.499
Just 'cause I was
stupid enough to get shot.

01:03:52.500 --> 01:03:54.666
- Just keep driving.
- I'm not gonna let you die.

01:03:54.667 --> 01:03:56.874
Who said anything about dying?
Just go. Come on.

01:03:56.875 --> 01:03:58.416
[automated female voice]<i>Warning.</i>

01:03:58.417 --> 01:04:01.249
<i>Organ storage temperature
too high. Action required.</i>

01:04:01.250 --> 01:04:02.875
Why is it going up?

01:04:06.125 --> 01:04:07.707
- Is there a button?
- No.

01:04:07.708 --> 01:04:09.957
It's the coolant. I told you
this thing's not bulletproof.

01:04:09.958 --> 01:04:11.749
- It got shot?
- If this thing gets to 9,

01:04:11.750 --> 01:04:13.207
we lose the viability.

01:04:13.208 --> 01:04:15.624
- How long do we have?
- We got 10 minutes.

01:04:15.625 --> 01:04:17.541
- That's not enough time.
- What?

01:04:17.542 --> 01:04:19.707
We're not gonna make it.
Either are you.

01:04:19.708 --> 01:04:21.041
Ben, I gotta pull over.

01:04:21.042 --> 01:04:22.707
[biker over radio]<i>Any word from our eyes</i>

01:04:22.708 --> 01:04:23.999
<i>in that hospital?</i>

01:04:24.000 --> 01:04:26.291
<i>I need their location now.</i>

01:04:26.292 --> 01:04:29.207
Now we know how they knew
we were at the concert venue.

01:04:29.208 --> 01:04:31.332
[tense music]

01:04:31.333 --> 01:04:33.624
Uh... take me
to the closest gas station.

01:04:33.625 --> 01:04:35.791
[automated voice] <i>Warning.
Organ storage temperature...</i>

01:04:35.792 --> 01:04:37.457
I know, lady! God!

01:04:37.458 --> 01:04:39.583
Ben's shot! I need some ice!
I just need...

01:04:40.208 --> 01:04:42.249
I need more time, man.
We need more time.

01:04:42.250 --> 01:04:43.541
Uh...

01:04:43.542 --> 01:04:45.166
Gotta call Kate.

01:04:45.167 --> 01:04:48.166
[cell phone ringing]

01:04:48.167 --> 01:04:49.291
Ben.

01:04:49.292 --> 01:04:50.791
[Hank] <i>Hey, Kate,
this is Hank Malone.</i>

01:04:50.792 --> 01:04:52.707
I know I promised
you something.

01:04:52.708 --> 01:04:54.332
I intend to keep that promise.

01:04:54.333 --> 01:04:56.332
<i>But I need you to do me
a favour. Can you help me out?</i>

01:04:56.333 --> 01:04:58.124
- OK.
- I'm gonna give you my location

01:04:58.125 --> 01:04:59.916
and a description
of the vehicle we're in.

01:04:59.917 --> 01:05:01.582
I need you to relay
that information

01:05:01.583 --> 01:05:03.332
to Dr Ainsley and her staff.

01:05:03.333 --> 01:05:05.582
Here's what I need
you to do - stay close by,

01:05:05.583 --> 01:05:07.749
<i>and watch if anybody
makes a call right after.</i>

01:05:07.750 --> 01:05:09.416
<i>- Can you do that?</i>
- [Kate] OK.

01:05:09.417 --> 01:05:12.457
Uh, we'll be... outside
the church in Tamborine,

01:05:12.458 --> 01:05:13.541
just off the main drag.

01:05:13.542 --> 01:05:15.583
<i>We'll be in a black Land Rover.</i>

01:05:18.708 --> 01:05:21.167
[dramatic music]

01:05:23.833 --> 01:05:25.999
- Hey, Ben? Ben?
- [automated voice] <i>Warning...</i>

01:05:26.000 --> 01:05:28.708
Hey, stay with me.
Hey, talk to me, buddy.

01:05:29.542 --> 01:05:31.374
[laboured panting]<i>Now</i> he wants me to talk.

01:05:31.375 --> 01:05:33.124
That's a twist.

01:05:33.125 --> 01:05:34.707
[winces]

01:05:34.708 --> 01:05:37.666
Ah, I finally got you
into bucket one.

01:05:37.667 --> 01:05:40.291
Remind me what
bucket one is, again?

01:05:40.292 --> 01:05:42.707
Drinking the
Ben Bishop Kool-Aid.

01:05:42.708 --> 01:05:44.041
[Hank chuckles]

01:05:44.042 --> 01:05:45.999
Ah, you know...

01:05:46.000 --> 01:05:47.791
I'm kinda leaning
into that, man.

01:05:47.792 --> 01:05:49.207
Leaning?

01:05:49.208 --> 01:05:51.457
I just saved your ass
back there.

01:05:51.458 --> 01:05:53.667
[wry chuckle]
What do I gotta do?

01:05:54.333 --> 01:05:55.957
Not die.

01:05:55.958 --> 01:05:58.167
I'm not gonna die in Australia.

01:06:01.833 --> 01:06:04.875
[biker] Tamborine Church?
That's just off the 95.

01:06:05.500 --> 01:06:08.666
They're at the church.
Route 95 in Tamborine!

01:06:08.667 --> 01:06:11.292
[dramatic music builds]

01:06:11.890 --> 01:06:14.348
All right, we're almost there,
buddy. Stay with me.

01:06:17.250 --> 01:06:18.708
[tires screech]

01:06:20.083 --> 01:06:22.292
[engines revving]

01:06:34.375 --> 01:06:37.958
[bullets ricocheting]

01:06:40.292 --> 01:06:41.457
[cocks gun]

01:06:41.458 --> 01:06:43.667
[dramatic music rises]

01:06:46.708 --> 01:06:48.083
[music subsides]

01:06:57.875 --> 01:06:59.499
- [entry bell tinkles]
- [Ben winces]

01:06:59.500 --> 01:07:01.749
Call an ambulance! Have them
come to the back of the store.

01:07:01.750 --> 01:07:03.124
The back, got it?

01:07:03.125 --> 01:07:05.416
Tell them this man's dying
from a gunshot wound.

01:07:05.417 --> 01:07:07.249
Then bring a bag of ice.

01:07:07.250 --> 01:07:08.666
- Do it!
- [Ben groans]

01:07:08.667 --> 01:07:10.416
- OK. Uh...
- [keypad beeping]

01:07:10.417 --> 01:07:12.249
- [Ben groaning]
- [automated voice] <i>Warning.</i>

01:07:12.250 --> 01:07:14.083
<i>Organ storage temperature
too high...</i>

01:07:14.750 --> 01:07:17.457
- There you go. Head on there.
- [Ben wincing]

01:07:17.458 --> 01:07:18.707
All right, let's see this.

01:07:18.708 --> 01:07:22.667
[Ben winces, moans]

01:07:26.167 --> 01:07:27.749
Hey, just put some
pressure on it.

01:07:27.750 --> 01:07:30.291
Ben, hold it. Put your hand--
You gotta keep pressure on it.

01:07:30.292 --> 01:07:31.541
Yeah?

01:07:31.542 --> 01:07:33.542
[inhales sharply]

01:07:35.708 --> 01:07:38.499
- Come on, Kate. Call me.
- Please, don't take your time.

01:07:38.500 --> 01:07:40.624
Why aren't you getting ice?!

01:07:40.625 --> 01:07:42.292
No, please...

01:07:50.917 --> 01:07:52.917
- Ice!
- Uh... right.

01:07:54.625 --> 01:07:57.292
[Ben winces] Tell me
the story about the bird.

01:07:58.250 --> 01:08:01.124
Spirit.
You said there's a story.

01:08:01.125 --> 01:08:02.957
[Ben groans]

01:08:02.958 --> 01:08:05.999
Uh... some rich guy was
trying to deliver it to his ex.

01:08:06.000 --> 01:08:07.499
She didn't want it.

01:08:07.500 --> 01:08:09.499
I was gonna take it
to animal control,

01:08:09.500 --> 01:08:11.291
but I got the call
to pick you up

01:08:11.292 --> 01:08:14.499
and didn't have time,
so I kept it with me.

01:08:14.500 --> 01:08:16.500
That's it?

01:08:18.083 --> 01:08:19.666
I didn't say
it was a <i>good</i> story.

01:08:19.667 --> 01:08:22.041
No, but you said
it was a long story,

01:08:22.042 --> 01:08:24.832
which makes you think
it's something interesting.

01:08:24.833 --> 01:08:26.874
That was just short and boring.

01:08:26.875 --> 01:08:29.749
All right,
you want me to tell it again,

01:08:29.750 --> 01:08:32.249
take my time with it, maybe
use a few more adjectives?

01:08:32.250 --> 01:08:34.041
- Yeah, tell it again.
- Ready?

01:08:34.042 --> 01:08:35.374
Yeah.

01:08:35.375 --> 01:08:37.291
But take your time with it--

01:08:37.292 --> 01:08:42.833
[Ben hollers]

01:08:43.667 --> 01:08:44.999
Long story.

01:08:45.000 --> 01:08:46.999
[breathing sharply]

01:08:47.000 --> 01:08:49.416
- OK. Here.
- [automated voice] <i>Warning.</i>

01:08:49.417 --> 01:08:51.416
<i>- Organ storage temperature...</i>
- I'm working on it!

01:08:51.417 --> 01:08:53.582
- Where's that ice?!
- Yeah, yeah, yeah! Coming!

01:08:53.583 --> 01:08:55.582
[automated voice] <i>Warning.
Organ storage temperature...</i>

01:08:55.583 --> 01:08:58.082
She's being passive aggressive.
[inhales sharply]

01:08:58.083 --> 01:09:00.250
- [winces]
- Put it right there.

01:09:01.125 --> 01:09:03.625
Maybe two hands, OK? You
gotta keep it from bleeding.

01:09:04.625 --> 01:09:06.582
I thought I'd done
all the hard stuff.

01:09:06.583 --> 01:09:08.416
[automated voice]<i>Organ storage temperature...</i>

01:09:08.417 --> 01:09:10.250
- Uh...
- [Ben] Hank? Hank?

01:09:10.875 --> 01:09:12.667
You gotta deal with that.

01:09:13.542 --> 01:09:16.167
[soft music]

01:09:16.917 --> 01:09:18.458
It's OK.

01:09:27.708 --> 01:09:29.124
What's the code?

01:09:29.125 --> 01:09:30.957
[panting heavily]

01:09:30.958 --> 01:09:34.042
It's pound, 3, 7, 2, 1, 5.

01:09:34.625 --> 01:09:35.833
[case pings]

01:09:40.333 --> 01:09:41.749
[automated voice] <i>Warning.</i>

01:09:41.750 --> 01:09:44.833
<i>Organ storage temperature
too high. Action required.</i>

01:09:49.583 --> 01:09:50.666
[keypad beeps]

01:09:50.667 --> 01:09:51.875
[case pings]

01:09:53.833 --> 01:09:54.917
[Hank sighs]

01:09:57.042 --> 01:09:58.500
[mutters]

01:10:00.875 --> 01:10:02.582
[clerk] <i>Uh, uh... mates!</i>

01:10:02.583 --> 01:10:05.624
Um... these guys
are coming with guns!

01:10:05.625 --> 01:10:08.666
- What do I do?
- [Hank] <i>Just relax! Act normal.</i>

01:10:08.667 --> 01:10:10.292
OK, relax. Act normal.

01:10:10.875 --> 01:10:12.832
Normal. I can do that.
[laughs nervously]

01:10:12.833 --> 01:10:15.000
[entry bell tinkles]

01:10:20.542 --> 01:10:22.041
Call that nurse.

01:10:22.042 --> 01:10:25.500
<i>Remind her what we'll do to her
family if she fucks this up.</i>

01:10:30.750 --> 01:10:32.916
[chuckling nervously]
Hi. Good day, mate.

01:10:32.917 --> 01:10:34.541
[stammering]
Is there maybe, like,

01:10:34.542 --> 01:10:36.249
something I can
help you with?

01:10:36.250 --> 01:10:39.291
[mocking] Uh, like-like-like,
for your sake,

01:10:39.292 --> 01:10:41.083
I fucking hope so.

01:10:47.250 --> 01:10:49.167
You look like
you want your momsy.

01:10:50.042 --> 01:10:52.708
Why do you look like
you want your momsy?

01:10:53.292 --> 01:10:54.833
No, I don't want my momsy.

01:10:56.125 --> 01:10:57.916
Well, then why
are you trembling?

01:10:57.917 --> 01:11:00.082
[voice quivering]
I'm... I'm not trembling.

01:11:00.083 --> 01:11:03.499
[sirens approaching]

01:11:03.500 --> 01:11:05.332
What the fuck is that shit,
then?!

01:11:05.333 --> 01:11:06.957
Oh, they're coming in!
They're coming in!

01:11:06.958 --> 01:11:08.292
[clerk yells]

01:11:09.708 --> 01:11:10.875
[biker] Come on, come on!

01:11:21.083 --> 01:11:22.792
[Hank grunts with effort]

01:11:24.708 --> 01:11:26.500
- [paramedic grunts]
- Gimme your keys.

01:11:29.417 --> 01:11:31.833
Later today, you'll realise
I'm one of the good guys.

01:11:34.333 --> 01:11:35.583
[sliding door closes]

01:11:36.792 --> 01:11:40.083
[weakly] It might take longer
than "later today".

01:11:47.083 --> 01:11:48.292
[horn blaring]

01:11:51.458 --> 01:11:54.667
[siren wails]

01:11:56.083 --> 01:11:57.207
[huffs]

01:11:57.208 --> 01:11:58.417
Go!

01:11:59.333 --> 01:12:00.917
[siren wailing]

01:12:04.417 --> 01:12:06.707
OK, you got this.
You've got this.

01:12:06.708 --> 01:12:08.541
Shh. That's it,
that's it, that's it.

01:12:08.542 --> 01:12:10.041
[monitor beeping rapidly]

01:12:10.042 --> 01:12:12.332
- [gasps] No, no, no, no...
- What the hell does that mean?

01:12:12.333 --> 01:12:15.041
He's gone into hypovolemic shock
and haemorrhaging internally.

01:12:15.042 --> 01:12:16.916
- I can't stop it.
- What do you mean, you can't--

01:12:16.917 --> 01:12:17.916
Do something!

01:12:17.917 --> 01:12:19.249
I'm administering saline,

01:12:19.250 --> 01:12:20.791
but he's bleeding
too heavily.

01:12:20.792 --> 01:12:23.207
His gastric artery ruptured.

01:12:23.208 --> 01:12:25.624
- [Hank] Is...?
- There's nothing else I can do.

01:12:25.625 --> 01:12:27.417
Hang in there, Ben.

01:12:31.958 --> 01:12:35.167
[monitor beeping steadily]

01:12:39.792 --> 01:12:42.917
[monitor beeping rapidly]

01:12:44.125 --> 01:12:45.416
[laboured breathing]

01:12:45.417 --> 01:12:46.582
[weakly] Hey, Hank...

01:12:46.583 --> 01:12:48.375
Yeah, yeah. I'm here, I'm here.

01:12:49.375 --> 01:12:51.167
When we get to Paris...

01:12:52.417 --> 01:12:54.750
...everyone's gonna say
get macarons.

01:12:55.833 --> 01:12:57.457
Tourist move.

01:12:57.458 --> 01:12:59.416
We're gonna go to Montmarte.

01:12:59.417 --> 01:13:01.332
We're gonna get choupettes.

01:13:01.333 --> 01:13:04.333
That's what a real Francophile
like Isabel would do.

01:13:04.917 --> 01:13:06.458
Trust me.

01:13:07.417 --> 01:13:09.042
Hank, trust me.

01:13:13.042 --> 01:13:14.582
Ben?

01:13:14.583 --> 01:13:16.666
[gentle ethereal vocalising]

01:13:16.667 --> 01:13:18.249
Ben?

01:13:18.250 --> 01:13:22.042
[monitor flatlining]

01:13:24.542 --> 01:13:28.917
[stirring music swells]

01:13:37.458 --> 01:13:38.583
[Hank] Ben.

01:13:43.083 --> 01:13:44.292
No...

01:13:46.250 --> 01:13:47.958
I'm so sorry, sir.

01:13:50.333 --> 01:13:52.000
He's gone.

01:14:06.833 --> 01:14:07.874
[guns firing]

01:14:07.875 --> 01:14:09.417
- [glass shatters]
- [gasps]

01:14:11.000 --> 01:14:12.082
[cocks gun]

01:14:12.083 --> 01:14:13.458
[fires]

01:14:14.583 --> 01:14:16.999
Can't let this piece of shit
get to the hospital.

01:14:17.000 --> 01:14:18.041
[cocks gun]

01:14:18.042 --> 01:14:20.458
[siren wailing]

01:14:25.042 --> 01:14:26.374
[gun fires]

01:14:26.375 --> 01:14:27.708
[cocks gun, fires]

01:14:31.000 --> 01:14:32.749
Gulf Charlie 4-11,
Gulf Charlie 4-11,

01:14:32.750 --> 01:14:34.124
urgent, urgent, shots fired.

01:14:34.125 --> 01:14:35.874
High-speed pursuit in progress.

01:14:35.875 --> 01:14:37.042
[sirens wail]

01:14:44.875 --> 01:14:46.666
Oh, come on, Hank.

01:14:46.667 --> 01:14:48.542
[siren wails]

01:14:49.583 --> 01:14:53.791
[cell phone ringing]

01:14:53.792 --> 01:14:55.957
Kate, it's a nurse!

01:14:55.958 --> 01:14:57.832
The person helping these people
is a nurse.

01:14:57.833 --> 01:15:00.332
Wait, what? A nurse?

01:15:00.333 --> 01:15:02.541
Yes. How many does Ellie have?

01:15:02.542 --> 01:15:04.874
I don't know, Hank.
There's a whole team.

01:15:04.875 --> 01:15:06.582
Do you have any other info?

01:15:06.583 --> 01:15:07.791
No.

01:15:07.792 --> 01:15:10.791
- Oh, shit.
- Julie?

01:15:10.792 --> 01:15:12.958
- Stop.
- [Hank] <i>Kate?</i>

01:15:13.958 --> 01:15:16.291
[Julie] This is 50 milligrams
of vecuronium.

01:15:16.292 --> 01:15:19.041
I promise it will be painless.

01:15:19.042 --> 01:15:20.667
Give me the phone, Kate.

01:15:22.292 --> 01:15:23.749
Fucking give it to me.

01:15:23.750 --> 01:15:25.708
[Julie on phone]<i>Close the curtain.</i>

01:15:32.167 --> 01:15:34.583
Get these cops off my arse.

01:15:35.500 --> 01:15:36.749
Come on, then!

01:15:36.750 --> 01:15:38.541
[bullets ricocheting]

01:15:38.542 --> 01:15:39.875
[tires screeching]

01:15:44.542 --> 01:15:45.958
[grunts angrily]

01:15:47.667 --> 01:15:51.208
[dramatic music continues]

01:16:00.375 --> 01:16:02.124
[grunts]
Undo the oxygen tank!

01:16:02.125 --> 01:16:03.625
[female paramedic] What?! Why?!

01:16:04.292 --> 01:16:06.417
[both grunting]

01:16:07.167 --> 01:16:08.207
Oh, fuck!

01:16:08.208 --> 01:16:09.666
[gun fires]

01:16:09.667 --> 01:16:11.249
[Hank] Now throw it
out the back.

01:16:11.250 --> 01:16:14.042
I will end you, peewee!

01:16:15.667 --> 01:16:17.333
[gunshot, glass shatters]

01:16:18.000 --> 01:16:19.625
[gunfire, sirens wailing]

01:16:21.583 --> 01:16:22.958
[female paramedic grunts]

01:16:27.958 --> 01:16:30.833
[traffic blaring]

01:16:32.458 --> 01:16:34.583
- [gunshot, glass shatters]
- [female paramedic screams]

01:16:35.958 --> 01:16:37.457
- [horn blares]
- Hang on!

01:16:37.458 --> 01:16:38.917
[tires screech]

01:16:41.958 --> 01:16:44.124
- Where are the flares?
- Why?

01:16:44.125 --> 01:16:45.416
Not a good time to explain!

01:16:45.417 --> 01:16:47.042
They're in the glove
compartment!

01:16:48.708 --> 01:16:50.250
[horns blaring]

01:16:51.542 --> 01:16:54.083
[dramatic music swells]

01:16:55.083 --> 01:16:56.917
[flare hissing]

01:16:58.167 --> 01:17:01.708
[screams]

01:17:03.250 --> 01:17:04.833
[music fades]

01:17:10.833 --> 01:17:12.541
[Kate]
How does it work, Julie?

01:17:12.542 --> 01:17:14.457
You just keep tabs
on the donor list

01:17:14.458 --> 01:17:16.041
and then call
the highest bidder?

01:17:16.042 --> 01:17:17.624
You think this is about money?

01:17:17.625 --> 01:17:19.707
You're talking about
killing a child.

01:17:19.708 --> 01:17:21.791
- Stop, Kate. Just shut up.
- My child!

01:17:21.792 --> 01:17:23.707
Just sit down or something.
You don't understand, OK?

01:17:23.708 --> 01:17:24.874
Just please be quiet.

01:17:24.875 --> 01:17:27.207
- How much, Julie?!
- I swear to God, Kate!

01:17:27.208 --> 01:17:28.957
How much is
my daughter's life worth?!

01:17:28.958 --> 01:17:31.666
Don't push me!
I swear to God...

01:17:31.667 --> 01:17:33.458
Just...

01:17:34.208 --> 01:17:35.625
Shit.

01:17:36.542 --> 01:17:38.375
[crying] I'm sorry.

01:17:40.875 --> 01:17:42.917
They have my brother.

01:18:09.042 --> 01:18:11.332
Somebody help me! We've been
hijacked... I... [stammers]

01:18:11.333 --> 01:18:12.791
- That's him!
- [security guard] Freeze!

01:18:12.792 --> 01:18:14.082
- Listen--
- Freeze!

01:18:14.083 --> 01:18:15.541
- Whoa, whoa, listen!
- On the ground!

01:18:15.542 --> 01:18:17.874
No, listen to me! This is
for Ellie Baker's transplant!

01:18:17.875 --> 01:18:20.292
Not gonna ask you again!
GET ON THE GROUND!

01:18:21.125 --> 01:18:23.374
Is that Hank Malone?!
Lower your weapons!

01:18:23.375 --> 01:18:27.000
Lower them!
Mr Malone, please follow me.

01:18:30.000 --> 01:18:33.082
I'm talking about
my brother, OK?

01:18:33.083 --> 01:18:35.541
He's a surgeon,
and they've taken him,

01:18:35.542 --> 01:18:37.624
and they're forcing him
to do the procedure

01:18:37.625 --> 01:18:39.250
on Donna Zaldívar.

01:18:40.292 --> 01:18:43.167
I'm really sorry, Kate,
but I don't have a choice.

01:18:44.583 --> 01:18:45.749
How's she doing?

01:18:45.750 --> 01:18:47.457
She's good.
She's hanging in there.

01:18:47.458 --> 01:18:49.499
She's prepped
and ready for surgery.

01:18:49.500 --> 01:18:50.957
[nurse] He's got a gun!

01:18:50.958 --> 01:18:54.124
[menacing music rises]

01:18:54.125 --> 01:18:57.792
You come for the king,
you better not fucking miss.

01:18:59.792 --> 01:19:01.499
[distant gunfire]

01:19:01.500 --> 01:19:03.583
[both grunting]

01:19:04.500 --> 01:19:06.875
[menacing music swells]

01:19:08.500 --> 01:19:09.582
[both exclaiming]

01:19:09.583 --> 01:19:12.000
[groaning]

01:19:13.458 --> 01:19:14.833
Uh-oh.

01:19:22.458 --> 01:19:23.875
[grunting]

01:19:29.750 --> 01:19:33.292
- [Damián muttering]
- [door rattling]

01:19:36.167 --> 01:19:38.000
You're gonna hide now?

01:19:39.375 --> 01:19:41.249
I thought you wanted
to have a beer?

01:19:41.250 --> 01:19:42.916
[tapping on door]

01:19:42.917 --> 01:19:44.458
No?

01:19:45.625 --> 01:19:47.500
I've got the case.

01:19:50.625 --> 01:19:52.167
OK.

01:19:52.792 --> 01:19:53.958
[sighs]

01:19:57.833 --> 01:19:59.625
[both grunting, straining]

01:20:04.375 --> 01:20:06.417
You're losing a lot of blood,
Mr Malone.

01:20:08.500 --> 01:20:10.208
I have plenty left.

01:20:12.875 --> 01:20:15.957
[tense, dramatic music swells]

01:20:15.958 --> 01:20:18.167
[both straining]

01:20:19.083 --> 01:20:20.082
Put the gun--!

01:20:20.083 --> 01:20:21.792
[gunshots ring out]

01:20:24.417 --> 01:20:25.667
[moans weakly]

01:20:26.583 --> 01:20:27.958
[security guard]
Hey! Put the--

01:20:29.917 --> 01:20:31.292
[gasps]

01:20:32.958 --> 01:20:36.458
[muttering angrily in Spanish]

01:20:37.583 --> 01:20:39.250
You piece of shit!

01:20:39.917 --> 01:20:42.582
[woman] <i>Oh, my God!
He shot a security guard!</i>

01:20:42.583 --> 01:20:44.874
<i>Run! Run!</i>

01:20:44.875 --> 01:20:48.957
[tense music escalates]

01:20:48.958 --> 01:20:50.500
[Kate grunts forcefully]

01:20:51.292 --> 01:20:54.875
[screaming]

01:20:59.875 --> 01:21:01.499
- You fucking bitch--
- [exclaims]

01:21:01.500 --> 01:21:02.582
[Damián grunts]

01:21:02.583 --> 01:21:04.417
[both grunting]

01:21:05.375 --> 01:21:07.250
[strains with exertion]

01:21:15.333 --> 01:21:19.000
[PA announcer] <i>Emergency -
please evacuate the building.</i>

01:21:21.083 --> 01:21:22.250
[Damián grunts]

01:21:23.250 --> 01:21:24.375
[groans]

01:21:32.542 --> 01:21:34.957
I'd offer to split it
with you, but...

01:21:34.958 --> 01:21:36.874
one of us is gonna
have to die today.

01:21:36.875 --> 01:21:38.042
Oh, yeah?

01:21:38.833 --> 01:21:40.167
You.

01:21:43.542 --> 01:21:45.583
[glass smashing]

01:21:47.042 --> 01:21:49.500
[both grunting]

01:22:00.208 --> 01:22:01.749
[automated female voice]<i>Warning.</i>

01:22:01.750 --> 01:22:04.832
<i>Organ storage temperature
too high. Action required.</i>

01:22:04.833 --> 01:22:08.833
[dramatic music swells]

01:22:12.375 --> 01:22:13.583
[Kate grunts]

01:22:15.042 --> 01:22:17.874
<i>Warning. Organ storage
temperature too high.</i>

01:22:17.875 --> 01:22:19.125
<i>Action required.</i>

01:22:24.292 --> 01:22:25.333
[Kate groans]

01:22:31.250 --> 01:22:32.791
[glass shattering]

01:22:32.792 --> 01:22:36.291
[groans, pants]

01:22:36.292 --> 01:22:37.999
[laughs]

01:22:38.000 --> 01:22:40.292
[PA announcer] <i>Emergency -
please evacuate the building.</i>

01:22:45.750 --> 01:22:46.833
[Hank grunts]

01:22:48.583 --> 01:22:49.875
[hollers]

01:22:52.583 --> 01:22:54.458
[electricity sparking]

01:22:57.583 --> 01:22:59.166
[objects crashing]

01:22:59.167 --> 01:23:00.542
[glass shattering]

01:23:07.000 --> 01:23:08.416
[automated voice] <i>Warning.</i>

01:23:08.417 --> 01:23:11.167
<i>Organ storage temperature
too high. Action required.</i>

01:23:12.542 --> 01:23:14.792
- [Damián grunting]
- [Hank groans]

01:23:16.542 --> 01:23:17.874
[exclaims]

01:23:17.875 --> 01:23:20.541
[grunting]

01:23:20.542 --> 01:23:23.625
[dramatic music continues]

01:23:30.583 --> 01:23:32.541
- [loud thudding]
- [Kate yelps]

01:23:32.542 --> 01:23:34.249
[vapour hissing]

01:23:34.250 --> 01:23:35.957
[gasps]

01:23:35.958 --> 01:23:38.667
[Hank and Damián grunting]

01:23:39.458 --> 01:23:40.708
[both groaning]

01:23:42.708 --> 01:23:43.833
[winces]

01:23:44.500 --> 01:23:47.250
[Kate] Help! Somebody!

01:23:48.667 --> 01:23:51.124
[PA announcer] <i>E -
please evacuate the building.</i>

01:23:51.125 --> 01:23:52.749
Oh, wait, wait, wait.

01:23:52.750 --> 01:23:53.874
[panting]

01:23:53.875 --> 01:23:55.167
I need a minute.

01:23:56.042 --> 01:23:57.292
Let's take a break.

01:23:58.500 --> 01:24:00.749
[Damián chuckles]

01:24:00.750 --> 01:24:01.832
[Kate] Help!

01:24:01.833 --> 01:24:04.208
[laughs]

01:24:05.542 --> 01:24:07.291
That's fair.

01:24:07.292 --> 01:24:10.166
[speaks in Portuguese]

01:24:10.167 --> 01:24:12.124
- [Hank chuckles warily]
- [automated voice] <i>Warning.</i>

01:24:12.125 --> 01:24:14.832
<i>Organ storage temperature
too high. Action required.</i>

01:24:14.833 --> 01:24:16.792
Yeah, whatever you said.

01:24:18.958 --> 01:24:21.083
Please, please, please,
please, please.

01:24:22.208 --> 01:24:23.957
[menacing music builds]

01:24:23.958 --> 01:24:25.250
[strains]

01:24:25.700 --> 01:24:26.909
Hey.

01:24:28.708 --> 01:24:30.291
[whimpers]

01:24:30.292 --> 01:24:31.458
Hey!

01:24:32.583 --> 01:24:34.042
[screams]

01:24:36.500 --> 01:24:38.708
Please... [whimpers]

01:24:40.833 --> 01:24:42.541
I'm sorry.

01:24:42.542 --> 01:24:44.125
[Kate] No. [groans]

01:24:49.667 --> 01:24:51.082
[automated voice] <i>Warning.</i>

01:24:51.083 --> 01:24:53.792
<i>Organ storage temperature
too high. Action required.</i>

01:24:55.750 --> 01:24:57.249
[gun cocking]

01:24:57.250 --> 01:25:00.417
Wait, wait, wait, wait.
Don't shoot yet.

01:25:04.333 --> 01:25:05.957
You like countdowns, right?

01:25:05.958 --> 01:25:07.749
Yeah.

01:25:07.750 --> 01:25:10.124
You've done two today.
It's like...

01:25:10.125 --> 01:25:13.250
Kinda like your
signature thing. Yeah?

01:25:14.000 --> 01:25:17.749
- How 'bout I kick one off?
- [Damián] OK. All right.

01:25:17.750 --> 01:25:19.416
I'll start with three.

01:25:19.417 --> 01:25:21.083
Three.

01:25:22.417 --> 01:25:24.082
"Two."

01:25:24.083 --> 01:25:25.916
[Hank] Don't rush me.

01:25:25.917 --> 01:25:27.499
[panting heavily]

01:25:27.500 --> 01:25:29.250
Two.

01:25:30.458 --> 01:25:32.374
Oh, you know what
I just thought of?

01:25:32.375 --> 01:25:33.500
What?

01:25:34.333 --> 01:25:37.250
Your mother's gonna die
in prison because of you.

01:25:38.875 --> 01:25:40.082
One!

01:25:40.083 --> 01:25:41.875
- [Kate grunts]
- [Damián moans]

01:25:44.458 --> 01:25:46.249
[splutters weakly]

01:25:46.250 --> 01:25:48.083
[groans]

01:25:50.125 --> 01:25:52.875
- [winces]
- [sombre music]

01:26:08.792 --> 01:26:10.207
[automated voice] <i>Warning.</i>

01:26:10.208 --> 01:26:12.875
<i>Organ storage temperature
too high. Action required.</i>

01:26:17.542 --> 01:26:19.791
[PA announcer] <i>Emergency -
please evacuate the building.</i>

01:26:19.792 --> 01:26:22.250
[screams] Help! Help!

01:26:23.000 --> 01:26:24.667
Help!

01:26:25.583 --> 01:26:27.166
Please hurry up! Please!

01:26:27.167 --> 01:26:28.666
[male officer]
This is the police!

01:26:28.667 --> 01:26:32.000
[sirens wailing]

01:26:43.833 --> 01:26:45.375
[music fades]

01:26:53.458 --> 01:26:55.542
Hi, sweetheart.

01:26:57.375 --> 01:26:59.749
Can we go home now?

01:26:59.750 --> 01:27:01.333
[laughing] Yeah!

01:27:02.833 --> 01:27:04.583
[Dr Ainsley] Are we awake?

01:27:06.333 --> 01:27:09.458
I have a patient here
who wants to say hello.

01:27:13.333 --> 01:27:15.082
I'll leave you to it.

01:27:15.083 --> 01:27:16.458
Thank you.

01:27:18.750 --> 01:27:20.666
You weren't kidding, were you?

01:27:20.667 --> 01:27:22.208
About what?

01:27:22.917 --> 01:27:26.042
You are not a guy
people successfully mess with.

01:27:27.167 --> 01:27:28.749
[sighs fondly]

01:27:28.750 --> 01:27:29.875
[kisses]

01:27:31.042 --> 01:27:33.917
Thank you. Thank you.

01:27:35.042 --> 01:27:36.750
Um...

01:27:37.458 --> 01:27:39.291
I didn't know Ben Bishop,

01:27:39.292 --> 01:27:41.916
but he must have been
a really, really decent man.

01:27:41.917 --> 01:27:43.292
I'm so sorry.

01:27:45.042 --> 01:27:46.333
Ah.

01:27:48.667 --> 01:27:50.624
A doc said
a lucky lady in Sydney

01:27:50.625 --> 01:27:52.625
got a new heart
because of him.

01:27:53.875 --> 01:27:55.124
[sniffles]

01:27:55.125 --> 01:27:57.500
Well, he had a helluva heart.

01:27:58.500 --> 01:28:00.292
Yeah, he did.

01:28:01.333 --> 01:28:04.541
You're too big for that
wheelchair, did you know that?

01:28:04.542 --> 01:28:06.791
- [chuckles]
- [Hank] What?

01:28:06.792 --> 01:28:08.541
[Kate laughs]

01:28:08.542 --> 01:28:12.207
You know, it did feel
a little snug when I sat down.

01:28:12.208 --> 01:28:14.458
[Kate chuckles]

01:28:15.083 --> 01:28:17.082
Do you wanna play 21 questions?

01:28:17.083 --> 01:28:19.957
I have been wheeling
around this hospital

01:28:19.958 --> 01:28:22.916
in this tiny wheelchair,
so bored,

01:28:22.917 --> 01:28:25.124
wondering if someone
was gonna ask me that.

01:28:25.125 --> 01:28:26.667
[giggles]

01:28:28.000 --> 01:28:29.792
Are you a daddy?

01:28:31.750 --> 01:28:33.292
I was.

01:28:33.917 --> 01:28:35.832
I had a little girl.

01:28:35.833 --> 01:28:37.500
What was her name?

01:28:39.792 --> 01:28:41.166
Isabel.

01:28:41.167 --> 01:28:43.833
I think that name is pretty.

01:28:45.625 --> 01:28:47.208
I do too.

01:28:48.667 --> 01:28:52.374
OK. Let's do this. Are we
gonna play or we gonna play?

01:28:52.375 --> 01:28:54.499
- Yep.
- OK.

01:28:54.500 --> 01:28:56.916
Is it manmade?

01:28:56.917 --> 01:28:58.707
- Yes.
- It is?

01:28:58.708 --> 01:29:00.750
OK, is it...

01:29:01.708 --> 01:29:03.625
[pensive acoustic guitar]

01:29:08.500 --> 01:29:12.457
<i>♪ I still leave a place
for you at the table ♪</i>

01:29:12.458 --> 01:29:14.083
[horns tooting]

01:29:15.042 --> 01:29:18.417
<i>♪ Even though
your chair stays cold ♪</i>

01:29:20.333 --> 01:29:21.666
[Hank] <i>Merci.</i>

01:29:21.667 --> 01:29:24.749
<i>♪ Your laugh still lives
in these kitchen walls ♪</i>

01:29:24.750 --> 01:29:28.124
<i>♪ Oh, all the memories
they hold ♪</i>

01:29:28.125 --> 01:29:29.917
Great rec, Ben.

01:29:33.667 --> 01:29:36.749
<i>♪ Echoes ♪</i>

01:29:36.750 --> 01:29:38.666
<i>♪ That never get old ♪</i>

01:29:38.667 --> 01:29:41.041
[female voice, on app] <i>The cat
prefers museums in the spring.</i>

01:29:41.042 --> 01:29:43.375
Le chat préfère
les musées au printemps.

01:29:44.458 --> 01:29:48.667
<i>♪ Alone ♪</i>

01:29:56.292 --> 01:30:00.375
<i>♪ Alone ♪</i>

01:30:01.292 --> 01:30:04.666
<i>♪ When I'm all alone ♪</i>

01:30:04.667 --> 01:30:07.457
<i>♪ I talk to ghosts ♪</i>

01:30:07.458 --> 01:30:10.583
<i>♪ Trying to find you
in the quiet ♪</i>

01:30:14.000 --> 01:30:16.874
<i>♪ I play your song ♪</i>

01:30:16.875 --> 01:30:20.124
<i>♪ And pretend you're not gone ♪</i>

01:30:20.125 --> 01:30:23.000
<i>♪ And act like I'm not crying ♪</i>

01:30:24.125 --> 01:30:27.166
<i>♪ The only way I get this far ♪</i>

01:30:27.167 --> 01:30:31.082
<i>♪ The only way
I feel your heart ♪</i>

01:30:31.083 --> 01:30:34.042
[in French]

01:30:35.167 --> 01:30:37.708
<i>♪ Is letting mine... ♪</i>

01:30:40.000 --> 01:30:41.667
<i>♪ Break ♪</i>

01:30:42.458 --> 01:30:44.708
<i>♪ Until I see you ♪</i>

01:30:45.292 --> 01:30:47.333
<i>♪ Until I see you ♪</i>

01:30:48.417 --> 01:30:50.500
<i>♪ Until I see you ♪</i>

01:30:51.583 --> 01:30:54.832
<i>♪ Face to face ♪</i>

01:30:54.833 --> 01:30:57.499
<i>♪ Until I see you ♪</i>

01:30:57.500 --> 01:31:00.666
<i>♪ Until
I see you ♪</i>

01:31:00.667 --> 01:31:02.833
<i>♪ Until I see you ♪</i>

01:31:04.083 --> 01:31:06.208
<i>♪ Face to face ♪</i>

01:31:07.250 --> 01:31:10.082
<i>♪ Until I see you ♪</i>

01:31:10.083 --> 01:31:12.250
<i>♪ Until
I see you ♪</i>

01:31:13.250 --> 01:31:16.457
<i>♪ Until I see you ♪</i>

01:31:16.458 --> 01:31:19.082
<i>♪ Face to face. ♪</i>

01:31:19.083 --> 01:31:20.417
[song ends]

01:31:21.125 --> 01:31:24.250
[poignant atmospheric music]

01:31:48.708 --> 01:31:51.625
[haunting vocalising]

01:33:03.625 --> 01:33:05.458
[music swells]

01:34:13.250 --> 01:34:15.375
[dramatic music]

01:38:23.208 --> 01:38:25.000
[music fades out]
